{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects","id":42951,"title":"Lunars: Castes or Aspects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-05T10:06:28-08:00","id":42951,"title":"Lunars: Castes or Aspects","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=42899#post42899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if that means Lunars should have Aspects instead of Castes?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=42946#post42946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would like to see this discussed in its own thread. It sounds extremely promising.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per request of the Dev, this question has it's own thread.<br /> <br /> To give a bit of context, about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=42884#post42884\">here</a> in the Create a Lunar Trio thread, there was some discussion as to whether the Lunar castes were at all useful. People were observing that most castes give you a general role and the capability to carry out the tasks of that role, be they mental, physical, or social. The Lunar castes however, just give you the ability to carry out any task associated with one type of attributes.<br /> <br /> This sounded a bit more Aspect-like to me, so I asked the question.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, give us your thoughts on the following two questions in this thread:<br /> <br /> 1) What's the difference between Castes and Aspects?<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> 2) Should Lunars have Aspects instead of Castes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:17:51-08:00","id":42962,"title":"","content":"For the Dragon-Blooded, we've been told that they are actually five different kinds of Terrestrial Exalted who are similar enough to interbreed and learn each other's Charms. So &quot;Aspect&quot; could mean &quot;Host within the Host.&quot; (Host being my preferred in-setting term for &quot;Exalted splat&quot;.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:24:10-08:00","id":42970,"title":"","content":"Castes are limited synergies of splat powers that are aimed towards a specific goal.<br /> Aspects are different expressions of power within the same splat. In the case of Dragon-Blooded, Aspect and Favoured Abilities are secondary to the elemental powers of individual charms. For the moment, I expect Liminals to work the same way.<br /> <br /> On a design level, you could have Lunar Aspects based on their Totems and have the totems apply differently to each charm. However, it would be impossible to accomplish in practice, as there would be far too many Totems to account for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:28:38-08:00","id":42980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=42962#post42962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Dragon-Blooded, we've been told that they are actually five different kinds of Terrestrial Exalted who are similar enough to interbreed and learn each other's Charms. So &quot;Aspect&quot; could mean &quot;Host within the Host.&quot; (Host being my preferred in-setting term for &quot;Exalted splat&quot;.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Given the very individual origins of each Liminal Exalt, perhaps they have Aspects because they are not all entirely the same? Well, they do share the source that is the Dark Mother, and each Aspect shares a different source which were the emotions that went into making them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:33:58-08:00","id":42985,"title":"","content":"It is a good damn question.<br /> <br /> 1. Aspects are just what we called Terrestrial Castes, because functionally they are identical. This... should change. There is no reason to give Terrestrials castes and call them something else. Castes for Abilities, Aspects for Attributes? I like this, as it seems to relate to every Lunar being an aspect of the ever-changing Luna, if only rhetorically. Calling them Aspects might adapt our thinking. Others have proposed eliminating Lunar Castes- if instead folks were arranging their characters under Luna's aspects (Argent Madonna, Huntess, etc) it might break Lunars from Ass-Beater, Smart-Guy, Manipulator roles. Huntress might be Dexterity, Stamina, Perception, for example.<br /> <br /> 2. Hell if I know? I think that Lunars need to change. I think that Alchemicals demonstrate that Attribute-based exalts can operate very well. I think removing Lunars from three areas of over-specialization will only do them good. Castes/aspects can be viewed as shackles, they can also be archetypes. I think they need to be re-arranged a bit. A part of me thinks they should have no aspects/Castes. Another part thinks they should represent some archetype derived from Luna's many faces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1199-mister-lion","name":"Mister Lion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:37:30-08:00","id":42990,"title":"","content":"As a note, the devs have stated that Liminals have Aspects, not castes. I want to say that they posted a working definition of the difference at some point, but I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:53:37-08:00","id":43003,"title":"","content":"Perhaps for Lunars, each charm bought has 3 linked mental /social / physical benefits and your aspect boosts one of those benefits? Or for each charm you can buy one of the three flavours of effects cheaper and get the others for reduced costs? Just throwing random ideas out there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1794-doran","name":"doran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T11:06:41-08:00","id":43010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=42970#post42970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Castes are limited synergies of splat powers that are aimed towards a specific goal.<br /> Aspects are different expressions of power within the same splat. In the case of Dragon-Blooded, Aspect and Favoured Abilities are secondary to the elemental powers of individual charms. For the moment, I expect Liminals to work the same way. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to be the big one for me. It appears Aspects do more than your favoreds and anima, it actually impacts your personality, your Great Curse, and even how the same Charm amongst you and your peers expresses. Aspects, despite the term seeming less loose as they don't define roles, seem to define a bit more than a Caste does.<br /> <br /> Castes, by contrast, tend to be archetypal. They present a task that an Exalt excels. Or in the case of Sidereals, the most &quot;Aspect-like&quot; due to soem of their Charms, favor a suite of Charms that allow them to accomplish certain roles. <br /> <br /> Lunars fit Caste in this a tad better. It's not quite as much a job, mind, but still has the archetype of warrior, trickster, shaman or however else they want to define them. Full Moons will still be fighty, Changing Moons will likely have a lot of guile, and No Moons will be clever. And there will be mix and match of those. That a No Moon learns a Charm or a Full Moon won't change how it functions, though might change how it's implemented. And while Lunars are a group of outsiders and iconiclasts, there's some broad range in what can be done with &quot;physical dude.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=42970#post42970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... On a design level, you could have Lunar Aspects based on their Totems and have the totems apply differently to each charm. However, it would be impossible to accomplish in practice, as there would be far too many Totems to account for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think spirit shapes do a lot to kind of dampen the issues iwth Lunar Castes. The Castes are there kind of as an archetype, but I do not think it'd hurt if they were just not as strong as other Exalts (less xp difference between favored/not for instance). I think the idea that Castes are roles, but they've been dampened due to the purposeful breaking we appear to be getting in 3e, might be interesting. In the First Age the Castes meant more. In this Age, they don't as much due to design, not failure in their original setup.<br /> <br /> Spirit shapes then come in and they help customize. Charms that have effects based on your spirit shape besides DBT would not be a bad way to go, as it lets you get Terrestrial-like Aspects without having to actually have Aspects and in a way that is much broader than the Dragon-Blooded can do with five elements (although is also probably a circle of hell for the devs in that regard).<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T11:13:17-08:00","id":43016,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest question is actually this: What Castes or Aspects should Lunars even <i>have</i>? If Full Moon, Changing Moon and No Moon don't work, <i>why</i>? What <i>would </i>work, and why?<br /> <br /> <br /> Would making the three traditional Castes work be as simple as requiring you to choose only two of their Caste Attributes to favor, and then picking two out-of-Caste Attributes to favor? Or is there something still lacking in the three archetypes of &quot;physical hero&quot;, &quot;social hero&quot; and &quot;smart hero&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> And, of course, given that Totem would be the more important choice that one makes before Caste/Aspect and which ought to determine your Caste or Aspect, does the existence of the Totem make Caste/Aspect redundant?<br /> <br /> Would avoiding that redundancy require making the Totem come from the Caste instead, such as by having the Predator Caste, Scavenger Caste, or Herbivore Caste?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T11:17:45-08:00","id":43019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=42990#post42990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note, the devs have stated that Liminals have Aspects, not castes. I want to say that they posted a working definition of the difference at some point, but I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure this came up before, too... The closest I've found is this:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Q: Here's a question for Hatewheel et al.: do Liminals have caste marks and anima banners? <b>(DarckRedd)</b></i><br /> <br /> A: They have aspects and anima banners. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Identifying that one needs a caste to have a caste mark is all well and good, but we still need the distinction between Caste and Aspect. I'm kinda clueless; I'd honestly thought it was something about the nature of one's physical body (which would fit Dragonblooded, Liminals, and Alchemicals). Then I remembered Alchemicals have Castes, not Aspects, and binned the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T11:18:19-08:00","id":43020,"title":"","content":"Predator and Scavenger work. I'd add something for Trickster and Animal Magnetism. Maybe Migratory.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have a cool word for livestock? Livestock animals are really important as symbols of life, health and civilization.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T11:24:36-08:00","id":43024,"title":"","content":"The way I think of it is that Aspects reflect something inborn and bodily, while Castes reflect something about your personality and the role your patron deity imagines you serving. In the case of Lunar Castes you can replace &quot;patron deity&quot; with &quot;the Lunars who changed the castes&quot;, I guess. It feels to me like Aspect is something that bleeds into your nature unbidden, whereas Caste is more the result of an Incarna saying, &quot;My Chosen should be people like this.&quot; (Caste also implies a social division during the Primordial War and First Age, but Lunars are special since they changed theirs, and since the division of labour was never as rigid as the term implies, I'm not sure how different it would really be from &quot;We're posting you to monitor the pelagials because you're a Water Aspect&quot;.)<br /> <br /> Now, I do think you could draw a meaningful role division within the lines of the Lunar Caste Attributes, but I have to agree that the game hasn't done so to date. As a result, I don't think it would really <i>hurt</i> Lunars (relative to their current form) to give them Aspects, but it's hard to say which option is best overall. Caste implies a prescriptive framework and hints at a broader social structure and division of labour. Done right it emphasizes the Lunars as a host. Aspects are more like character quirks -- they say something about where the character comes from and emphasize the Exalt as individual. Lunars are the Exalted most associated with individuality, so that could be a good thing.<br /> <br /> While I don't have a strong sense of which option is better, I think I <i>prefer</i> castes, because I feel the Lunars need what sense of cohesion the game can give them, and I prefer how it interacts with un-tattooed Lunars' &quot;flexible subsplat&quot; gimmick: I prefer the idea of Lunars wearing many hats to the idea of Lunars being many hats (though the latter is legit since we're talking about Lunars).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 01-05-2014, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T11:50:01-08:00","id":43042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=42962#post42962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Dragon-Blooded, we've been told that they are actually five different kinds of Terrestrial Exalted who are similar enough to interbreed and learn each other's Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>When were we told that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister Lion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspects are just what we called Terrestrial Castes, because functionally they are identical. This... should change.</div> </div> </div> </div>With this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hatewheel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspect suggests a physical association, where Caste only suggests a predilection for certain kinds of action. It can be more complex than this, but this answer is the simplest version.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a functional delineation, and projections of detaching elemental associations with Aspect Abilities, it might be a good time to drop some of the more extraneous qualities of Aspect role proficiencies.<br /> <br /> Like, maybe play up more the wild passion of the Fire Aspect and play down the warrior-socialites.<br /> <br /> It's something we already see in characters like Ejava and Segezzer, neither of whom are really medics or rangers.<br /> <br /> On that note, I can actually see some of the merits of Lunars having Aspects instead; greater emphasis on difference in personality qualities and ways their powers and methods are expressed aesthetically rather than roles they play or aptitudes they display.<br /> <br /> Like a Full Moon Aspect who displays a lot of big, flashy, extreme passion ways of doing things (something that could readily intersect with warrior, trickster and shaman), while No Moons place more emphasis on being secretive and hidden, and Changing Moons are more a kind of balance in between, calculated exposure to manage responses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T11:52:00-08:00","id":43045,"title":"","content":"Aspect seems more.... primal? For me than Caste. Caste implied more of a 'job', a social position, while Aspect is more of 'what you are'?<br /> <br /> Regarding Spirit Shapes/Totems: I had an idea of using keywords to define animals/spirit shape. For example: a wolf from the North would have the following keywords: North, canine, predator. These keywords could show up among charms for added effect/xp-break on them (something I think the devs mentioned they were thinking about). Animals are already being designed with Lunars in mind, but adding these keywords can be done with a simple list even at a later date, and it helps making custom spirit shapes imho. Granted, this would mean a whole lot of new keywords probably...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T12:00:12-08:00","id":43048,"title":"","content":"I also feel as though Aspects makes more sense for Lunars than Castes. The Moon shifts through aspects or phases, never remaining in any fixed role. Luna herself has a number of different faces or aspects. It's a subtle change that implies something important about the nature of the Lunar Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T12:48:29-08:00","id":43069,"title":"","content":"I may not have everything down to the details so there may be some faults in the details of my grasp on the setting, but I'll go out on a limb and write down my view of it here.<br /> <br /> <b>1.</b> <b>Aspect</b> comes from drawing power of solid, graspable (&quot;physical&quot;) things.<br /> Dragon-Blooded channel the powers of the elements (of creation), the solid stuff that creation is built from/made up of. These are real, raw-materials. The same goes for Liminals who get/channel the power of what bodies are made up (the elements of the body); blood, flesh, sinew etc..<br /> In both these cases the different elements are symbiotic but different, and thus the host of that elemental group's Exalted will be divided into subgroups determined by which Aspect of the Head Group, the individual character has the strongest affinity for channeling (Be it Earth, Blood, Flesh etc.).<br /> The different Aspects of each Elemental Group all have different qualities and &quot;behaviours&quot;, resulting in them (the elements, but also the powers and charms based on them) materializing, acting and solving problems in different ways. Usually this means one individual element will be more effective in some things than others (usually stone will be harder to pass through than wind), and therefore mastering some skills/abilities will come easier to characters from one Aspect than to characters from another Aspect of the same Elemental group. In other words: the power you channel determine what your skills are (most) suited for.<br /> <br /> <b>Castes </b>comes from the intangible personality and power of a deity<br /> This power is not physical and are One and the same for all the members of the Host drawing power from it. However, since generalised growth without focus can lead to jack-of-all-trades-master-of-none-sydrome, the Gods have found it more efficient to divid up their followers into a caste system, to make them all focus their power (and growth) into a specialized Niche, that (mostly) complement eachother, to create a better/more &quot;powerful&quot; whole.<br /> <br /> <b>tl;dr</b><br /> <b>To Sum Up:</b> (my point of view) Aspects channel tangible aspects of the world. What the character is most suited to do comes from which power s/he has more affinity for/uses. (Restrictions are natural)<br /> Castes all channel the same, divine power, with much less finite possible applications. What the character has affinity for stems from a mold forced upon the character's exaltation. (Restrictions are synthetic).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>2.</b><br /> Coming from this view of what Caste contra Aspect is, I would have to say that I am torn..<br /> <b>First Thought;</b> Lunars should probably be forced into a caste system, simply in the name of symmetry, since they are Celestial Exalteds, However, If any Celestial Deity would defy, or break, that mould it would fit Luna.<br /> <b>Second Thought;</b> Since they draw upon the powers of Luna, they should have a caste-system to ensure synergy. But thinking over their powers and charms they seem more focused on the tangible things than magic feats. (making ones body strong enough to jump ten feet, rather than just &quot;magically&quot; doing it (the way Solars does it for instance).<br /> Thinking about how much of the Lunar-idea relates to and deals (almost exclusively) with the tangible world, albeit in a magical fashion, (that is to say, they deal, almost soley, with the physical but in the Way that their Patron Luna would do it?) makes me think that, maybe Aspect Lunars Would be a really nice idea. If there was to be a Hybrid of the two, they would Certainly fit the bill the best out of the current line-up of Hosts. But:<br /> <b>Third Thought:</b> What would those Aspects be?<br /> I really love the idea of them having Attributes as the source of their charms (but unfortunatley I don't think it has been implemented very well yet), but what aspects of bodies could be found that are as tangible as needed while still being ethereal enough to resonate with the Idea of Luna? If none can be found I'd say that'd be a problem for them having Aspects, but I've grown fond of the idea. It seems like Celestial Aspects could be such an Awesome and Powerful idea (fun fact; take the &quot;A&quot; from &quot;Awesome&quot; and &quot;P&quot; from &quot;Powerful&quot;, mix them together and spell them out backwards and you get &quot;Lunars&quot;)<br /> <br /> Well, I guess Lunar-Aspects could be something along the lines of Mind, Body, Heart and Soul. Of which only the Body is one we really associate wit hsomething tangible, while the others have tangible counterparts, that we do not associate fully with implications of them (the actual heart is not our emoions, and the Mind is not neccisarily reducable to the brain. The soul, of course, is actually a fact in the Setting). And then by mixing up which attributes are associated with which aspect you could get away from the Caste-yness of current Lunar Specification:<br /> Body could have Strength, Stamina and Appearance,<br /> Mind, Dexterity, Manipulation and Intelligence<br /> Heart, Charisma, Perception, Wits<br /> for instance. (soul I don't know, but of course there could be shared, or more limited aspect-attributes, depending on what one might think on).<br /> <br /> <b>To Sum Up:</b> I love the idea of Lunars, and their focus on the material world/bodies. Problem: I have been dissapointed of their implementations in the past, since I've not felt that they live up to my thoughts of their potential. Solution: Go nuts! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Don't hold back. there is no reason to feel restricted to maintaining what the Lunars is or has been up until now, since we can't know for sure what it is that's holding them back. After all, there is nothing that is less Lunar, than to adhere to restrictions, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T12:49:54-08:00","id":43070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43010#post43010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It appears Aspects do more than your favoreds and anima, it actually impacts your personality, your Great Curse, and even how the same Charm amongst you and your peers expresses. Aspects, despite the term seeming less loose as they don't define roles, seem to define a bit more than a Caste does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Totems likewise reflect their personalities, probably the specific form of their Great Curse, and may have some sort of impact on your Charms via keywords.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Castes, by contrast, tend to be archetypal. They present a task that an Exalt excels. </div> </div> </div>Except that the current three Lunar Castes don't have archetypical tasks. The Full Moon is just as easily a light-footed, sticky-fingered thief or a hardy and tireless laborer as a warrior. While various sources have made it out to be a &quot;Silver Dawn Caste&quot;, it's always lent itself to &quot;Silver Night Caste&quot; and &quot;Silver Zenith&quot; as well.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Alchemical Castes defy your definition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T12:53:10-08:00","id":43071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43020#post43020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Predator and Scavenger work. I'd add something for Trickster and Animal Magnetism. Maybe Migratory.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have a cool word for livestock? Livestock animals are really important as symbols of life, health and civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would these divisions even mean? What would it mean to have a Predator-aspected Totem? I don't see why it would impact the kind of Attributes you can favor, though I could see it providing a particular kind of Anima Effect and set of keywords (if keywords make it into the final product).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T12:59:54-08:00","id":43076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43042#post43042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When were we told that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Holden, in the previous forum. People were complaining about the Dragon-Blooded being the only Terrestrial Exalted, and Holden responded that the Dragon-Blooded were really more like five different hosts of interbreedable Terrestrial Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On that note, I can actually see some of the merits of Lunars having Aspects instead; greater emphasis on difference in personality qualities and ways their powers and methods are expressed aesthetically rather than roles they play or aptitudes they display.<br /> <br /> Like a Full Moon Aspect who displays a lot of big, flashy, extreme passion ways of doing things (something that could readily intersect with warrior, trickster and shaman), while No Moons place more emphasis on being secretive and hidden, and Changing Moons are more a kind of balance in between, calculated exposure to manage responses. </div> </div> </div>That would work in a set-up where Lunar Castes/Aspects are like Alchemical Castes.<br /> <br /> <br /> But where do the Totems come in? Totems are a big part of the Lunar's personality and concept -- second only in impact to a Devil Tiger's new Excellency and Charmset!<br /> <br /> If Totems are less important than Castes/Aspects, then how are they different from or more important than Solar anima icons?<br /> <br /> If Totems are more important than Castes/Aspects, then what is left for the Caste or Aspect to do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T13:02:21-08:00","id":43078,"title":"","content":"Here's another way to look at it:<br /> <br /> <b>Aspects: </b>Form<br /> <b>Castes:</b> Function","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T13:09:01-08:00","id":43083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43071#post43071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would these divisions even mean? What would it mean to have a Predator-aspected Totem? I don't see why it would impact the kind of Attributes you can favor, though I could see it providing a particular kind of Anima Effect and set of keywords (if keywords make it into the final product).</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it working like Dragon-Blooded Charms.<br /> <br /> For Example,<br /> <br /> <b>I Howl Really Loud Prana</b><br /> Requirements: Charisma ???<br /> <br /> You howl really loud and something happens.<br /> <br /> Predator Aspect: Nearby characters are forced out of stealth.<br /> Animal Magnetism Aspect: Nearby characters gain a minor positive intimacy towards you for the next action.<br /> Migratory: Nearby characters cannot be lost for the next of the scene.<br /> Livestock: Gain the benefits of a Defend Other action from any character in close or medium range.<br /> <br /> Or something to that effect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T13:14:09-08:00","id":43086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43070#post43070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunar Totems likewise reflect their personalities, probably the specific form of their Great Curse, and may have some sort of impact on your Charms via keywords.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why as I stated that I would think Castes initially but totems to help with Aspect-like qualites might be the way to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43070#post43070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that the current three Lunar Castes don't have archetypical tasks. The Full Moon is just as easily a light-footed, sticky-fingered thief or a hardy and tireless laborer as a warrior. While various sources have made it out to be a &quot;Silver Dawn Caste&quot;, it's always lent itself to &quot;Silver Night Caste&quot; and &quot;Silver Zenith&quot; as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their tasks are brute force dudes, guilish dudes and clever dudes more or less. This means there's bleed compared to the Solar Castes, such as how Chosen of Serenity overlap a bit with Eclipses, Zeniths and Twilights or Chosen of Secrets with Nights and Twilights.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that the <i>current</i> Caste smight actually be broad and not really as impactful as they were back in the day, but this is by teh choice of the inventors of the tattoos, not the original use of Castes back in the day. The breaking of the Castes allows for some flexibility in the nature of Lunar Castes that make them able to be very maleable and broad compared to other Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43070#post43070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, Alchemical Castes defy your definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Alchemical Caste section starts by outright saying Alchemical Castes are more like Terrestrial Aspects. I would argue that the latter probably does actually fit them better, but Alchemicals tend to actually be given jobs based on Caste and individual Charms don't seem to vary in effect much based on the Champion's composition. I don't remember anything at least like Dragon-Graced Weapon.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T13:14:54-08:00","id":43087,"title":"","content":"I honestly like they idea of aspect, I think it would fit the moon phases theme more","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T13:18:56-08:00","id":43092,"title":"","content":"Eh, so what is this Aspect vs Caste mumbu jumbo meant to mean in practise?<br /> <br /> Currently Lunars are set up so that you have to choose between being Physical, Social or Mental, this often ends up very akward as there are very few concepts that fit neatly into those boxes as contrasted by the Solars where the boxes are designed to fit very broad common archetypes. If you compare with the Dragonblooded their boxes are also slightly awkward but they have a clear theme to them and the fact they get 3 favoured abilities give you enough flexibility to fit most concepts.<br /> <br /> Really in my opinion with the Lunars is the lack of themes. In Physical they got their combat monster but beyond that Lunars are just a random mess of magical effects keyed of the attributes, there needs to be some sense of what your caste/aspect/whatever is supposed to achieve in the powerset.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T14:27:28-08:00","id":43127,"title":"","content":"More than anything, I'd love it if the Lunars got five Castes/Aspects in 3E. The three Castes idea was, frankly, a poor design choice from 1E that got carried over into 2E because . . . well, I don't know the because. Having only three Castes ironically pigeonholed Lunar characters, despite the broadness of the abilities they were given. While the Exalted Castes/Aspects could have just about any character concept applied to them and still work, the Lunar Castes were given limitations by being split between Physical, Mental, and Social. Even in 2E with Favored Attributes, it became difficult to flesh out a Lunar character beyond their general purpose. If you wanted to play a warrior, it was sub-optimal to not be a Full Moon. If you wanted to player a diplomat or trickster, it was sub-optimal not to play a Changing Moon. If you wanted to play a sorcerer or scholar, it was sub-optimal to not play a No Moon. Sure, the Solars &amp; DB's &amp; Sidereals have their warrior and diplomat and scholar classes delineated, you could still be a diplomatic Dawn or a scholarly Fire or a warrior Serenity. You were never told &quot;this is what you are&quot; because, despite a Caste/Aspect's leanings, you had enough wiggle room to play against type if you wanted to.<br /> <br /> The only redeeming factor with the Lunars in this regard is their shapeshifting. A full-on warrior could still have a mouse in his repertoire, allowing for stealth when needed. A sorcerous No Moon could still turn into a raging bull if it was time to smash or stampede. That's the only area of their capabilities that allowed them to stretch their legs a bit without being told &quot;that's not what you do.&quot;<br /> <br /> Whether Lunars get Aspects or Castes, they need better definition and less limitation. Give them five, open the Physical/Social/Mental Castes up a bit to concepts beyond Warrior/Socialite/Sorceror, and then you'll see a lot more characters who are a blend of ideas instead of a singular one pronounced in a different way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T14:43:48-08:00","id":43137,"title":"","content":"People talk about Full Moons being warriors, but Changing Moons get the Charms for training beasts and men, leading mass combat units, and psyching enemies out. No Moons got the Charms for hiding from all senses while sniffing out hiding enemies from the other side of a mountain and putting an arrow directly between their eyes <i>through </i>said mountain; also quick reflexes.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of combat Charms in social and mental Attributes, and plenty of physical Charms which aren't combative. Which just goes with what Saur Ops and I say about &quot;warrior&quot; being a mental task as well as a physical one. Dawn Castes get War for that reason!<br /> <br /> Is there a warrior Caste among the Alchemical Exalted? No. Each of the Alchemical Castes have their own approach to war - at most you can say that Orichalcums and Starmetals lend themselves more to warfare on a strategic level because of their Intelligence, whereas Moonsilvers and Jades are more tactical with their Wits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:06:11-08:00","id":43154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43092#post43092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, so what is this Aspect vs Caste mumbu jumbo meant to mean in practise?<br /> <br /> Currently Lunars are set up so that you have to choose between being Physical, Social or Mental, this often ends up very akward as there are very few concepts that fit neatly into those boxes as contrasted by the Solars where the boxes are designed to fit very broad common archetypes. If you compare with the Dragonblooded their boxes are also slightly awkward but they have a clear theme to them and the fact they get 3 favoured abilities give you enough flexibility to fit most concepts.<br /> <br /> Really in my opinion with the Lunars is the lack of themes. In Physical they got their combat monster but beyond that Lunars are just a random mess of magical effects keyed of the attributes, there needs to be some sense of what your caste/aspect/whatever is supposed to achieve in the powerset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps an option could be to tie it into their totem animal instead of three castes as it has been done up until now? The whole animal thing has always felt sort of slapped onto Lunars so I think it wouldn't hurt to give that a better reason for being there.<br /> <br /> For example, I'd say wolves are known for their endurance, for being social animals that live in packs, and for having keen senses, so a wolf totem could favor stamina, charisma and perception. Add in a fourth of your own choice based on your characters concept.<br /> <br /> Then again. it could become a bit too restrictive; are all owls wise and do all foxes have to be clever? Not to mention that different cultures around the world would not agree on the abilities for each animal. Should it be up to the player to define the animal or should there be a giant predefined list?<br /> <br /> I dunno. Just the first idea that appeared in my head while reading this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1837-show-us-your-commissions-2-the-revenge?p=23024#post23024\" target=\"_blank\">Lunar Art</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1508-sydriam","name":"Sydriam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1508_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:12:12-08:00","id":43156,"title":"","content":"We've only had one Exalt type that makes use of Aspects instead of Castes, and what really seems to set them apart from Caste-type Exalts is how their Aspect leaves a physical mark on them and flavors their Charms.<br /> <br /> For an Exalt type that is so focused on Shapeshifting and having utter control of their own selves, physical and mental? It doesn't make sense to me. They define what their bodies are and to think an Aspect could leave a mark on them that is outside of their control doesn't seem to fit. The only possible use of this is to tie it to the Tell, and that gets pretty restrictive I think.<br /> <br /> An Exalted type that would be better suited for Aspects would be the Alchemical Exalted, since they actually have an undeniable physical make-up (the magical material they're most made of). But even that has issues, honestly.<br /> <br /> From what we know, it doesn't make sense to me. I don't think it fits at all. And I would be disappointed if this change was made purely for the sake of making Lunars &quot;different&quot;.<br /> <br /> The only way I could see it, is if the Aspects are focused on Physical, Social and Mental. In which case... all we've really done is just changed the name of Castes to Aspects for no real reason. Which kinda makes the use of the word &quot;Castes&quot; over &quot;Aspects&quot; pretty damn pointless as the terms are clearly being used interchangeably.<br /> <br /> tldr: What's the point of this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:21:49-08:00","id":43161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43137#post43137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are plenty of combat Charms in social and mental Attributes, and plenty of physical Charms which aren't combative. Which just goes with what Saur Ops and I say about &quot;warrior&quot; being a mental task as well as a physical one. Dawn Castes get War for that reason!</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely here, it's the core of why Physical/Social/Mental doesn't work as a caste/aspect breakdown.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43137#post43137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People talk about Full Moons being warriors, but Changing Moons get the Charms for training beasts and men, leading mass combat units, and psyching enemies out. No Moons got the Charms for hiding from all senses while sniffing out hiding enemies from the other side of a mountain and putting an arrow directly between their eyes <i>through </i>said mountain; also quick reflexes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they get a random grabbag of effects along those lines but you can't actually build a Warleader Changing Moon or Sniper No Moon because there's no depth<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43137#post43137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a warrior Caste among the Alchemical Exalted? No. Each of the Alchemical Castes have their own approach to war - at most you can say that Orichalcums and Starmetals lend themselves more to warfare on a strategic level because of their Intelligence, whereas Moonsilvers and Jades are more tactical with their Wits.</div> </div> </div> </div>With 3 favoured attributes any alchemical can do pretty much whatever they want, the alchemical charm trees are also organised in such a way you can get actual depth into whatever you decide to specialise in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:26:39-08:00","id":43165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43137#post43137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are plenty of combat Charms in social and mental Attributes, and plenty of physical Charms which aren't combative. Which just goes with what Saur Ops and I say about &quot;warrior&quot; being a mental task as well as a physical one. Dawn Castes get War for that reason!<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>You can say that again. There may be more Combat charms in the mental attributes than there are 'Wisdom and Life' charms in the mental attributes, but that is a common enough of a nitpick.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Lunars could stand to have them all.<br /> <br /> They could have their Caste, their moonphase, the mark that appears on their brow which suggests the ultimate role of Luna's Chosen, Warrior, Sage, or Courtier.<br /> <br /> They could have their Totem, the bit of Creation that anchors them through their many travels between the worlds and marks their appearance as something more than human.<br /> <br /> They could have their Aspect, their patron's face. The portion of Luna's power that influences them more than any other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1787-vince","name":"Vince","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:34:55-08:00","id":43170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vince</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43165#post43165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could have their Caste, their moonphase, the mark that appears on their brow which suggests the ultimate role of Luna's Chosen, Warrior, Sage, or Courtier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one beef I have with organising the Lunars as Warrior/Courtier/Sage is that it makes them come across as Solars lite and just aping the Dawn/Twilight/Eclipse. Couldn't Lunars have something completely different like Brutality/Finesse/Guile or whatever, the different castes/aspects could have different means to achieve similar effects and all of them could fill the warrior/sage/courtier roles in a group but they'd do it differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:35:15-08:00","id":43172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43127#post43127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you wanted to play a warrior, it was sub-optimal to not be a Full Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you wanted to coordinate attacks or run a military apparatus, in which case Changing Moons and No Moons would be a better choice. Yes, you could conceivably pick another Attribute that could help, but that would only give you a limited in on that arena. Ask yourself, &quot;How much does it help being in charge of a military organization at some level of hierarchy to be able to vastly outpace, overpower and outlast the troops under your command?&quot;<br /> <br /> Full Moons would be dynamite special forces types or spies trusted with autonomy out in the field, but being in any position of authority which relies on the strength of others isn't playing to the Full Moon's being, whereas a Dawn could just learn War and be fine with all of the tasks that involve military organizations. This is why it's a mistake to think of Full Moons as being exactly like Dawns or filling even remotely similar roles. Additionally, those physical properties can have a lot of odd side benefits, such as using claws to climb or carve sculptures (that this option was not given is an issue of EX2's Silver Solar issue; even the poor execution of Lunars in EX1 offered a wider array of possibilities for dangerous body parts in its own fashion).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you wanted to player a diplomat or trickster, it was sub-optimal not to play a Changing Moon. If you wanted to play a sorcerer or scholar, it was sub-optimal to not play a No Moon. Sure, the Solars &amp; DB's &amp; Sidereals have their warrior and diplomat and scholar classes delineated, you could still be a diplomatic Dawn or a scholarly Fire or a warrior Serenity. You were never told &quot;this is what you are&quot; because, despite a Caste/Aspect's leanings, you had enough wiggle room to play against type if you wanted to. </div> </div> </div>You've full-on fallen into the same trap as the writer of the mortal splat chapter of Scroll of Heroes. If a Lunar Caste has an Attribute that gives you an advantage in an arena, it's a lucky accident. Their strengths aren't really meant to play to clearly defined roles, because while it'd be cool to be able to form plates of armor over your skin, bend light around you like the Predator or see fear, these aren't necessarily things that help all of the time if you're engaged in some form of employment, and relying on them isn't going to necessarily make you good at your job, because, again, with the military membership example, the armed forces don't want someone who can outperform all the other soldiers physically and make ammunition from shed skin. They value someone who can take orders and who won't go berserk if someone they care about more than the organization itself is injured or killed. By amassing many such people, and playing to their strengths, they win battles. If they invite on a dualistic shapeshifter that switches between virtuous and psycho at the drop of a hat... well, you probably get the idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only redeeming factor with the Lunars in this regard is their shapeshifting. A full-on warrior could still have a mouse in his repertoire, allowing for stealth when needed. A sorcerous No Moon could still turn into a raging bull if it was time to smash or stampede. That's the only area of their capabilities that allowed them to stretch their legs a bit without being told &quot;that's not what you do.&quot;<br /> <br /> Whether Lunars get Aspects or Castes, they need better definition and less limitation. Give them five, open the Physical/Social/Mental Castes up a bit to concepts beyond Warrior/Socialite/Sorceror, and then you'll see a lot more characters who are a blend of ideas instead of a singular one pronounced in a different way. </div> </div> </div>Don't even consider what you do. With Lunars, concentrate on what a member of each Caste is. The process will be profoundly different from Ability-based Exalted, but that's the point of the exercise. If it's that off-putting, you might not actually like Lunars. There's nothing wrong with that, but the Lunars shouldn't be bent around to be similar to other Exalted for any reason. That was done in EX2, and it didn't work out too well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:21:08-08:00","id":43198,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the Changing Moon and No Moon combat charms don't really have synergy with their other charms, nor do they have anything to do with the purported role of those Castes. Hell, No Moons are much better at stealth combat than they are at being shamans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:21:42-08:00","id":43199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sydriam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43154#post43154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps an option could be to tie it into their totem animal instead of three castes as it has been done up until now? The whole animal thing has always felt sort of slapped onto Lunars so I think it wouldn't hurt to give that a better reason for being there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The animal themes for Lunars come from their original WoD analogue being the Fera. They also draw on things like skinwalkers, werewolves, rakshasa, and other shapeshifting monsters in the dark. It also included trickster characters like Loki, Hanuman, Coyote, Crow and Ananasi, a few of whome have a very specific critter they became. This adds up to a good amount of bestial traits actually. They are also unique amongst the Exalted in that they draw on animal elements, something that helps distinguish their shared &quot;night&quot; themes with Abyssals and Sidereals, as well as makes them unique amongst the Exalted there.<br /> <br /> So the critter themes aren't bad in themselves, and never really were IMHO. They could maybe be a bit more impactful or interesting though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43156#post43156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what we know, it doesn't make sense to me. I don't think it fits at all. And I would be disappointed if this change was made purely for the sake of making Lunars &quot;different&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is worth highlighting in all of this and I kind of agree. It seems to me that the Caste/Aspect thing is ill-defined as-is. And what we do have of Aspects seems to require a bit of forcing to break Lunars out of Castes. Folks might not like Castes for Lunars, but it does fit in my view a bit more with them than Aspects as presented in Liminals and Terrestrails seem to (and to some extent the Caste-really-Aspect of Alchemicals does).<br /> <br /> The Caste issues for Lunars isn't so bad if:<br /> - The three we have are loose as hell and not really &quot;rolish&quot; by the designs of the Lunars, rather than by Luna.<br /> - There is an option to easily dip into other Castes with two or three favoreds ala Alchemicals. A Full Moon will always primarily be a hero defined by his physical puissance, but can have a bit of guile, cleverness or awareness as neeeded. The point of favoreds really. Maybe also making the cost for non-Caste not so bad.<br /> - Totems having some effect that they don't in prior editions, or emphasis on it, seem to me a better way to handle things while keeping the Castes, which are at least interesting in my mind than just tossing the idea out.<br /> <br /> Different for different's sake is an issue really. And tossing something out without first seeing what can be done to make it work seems to me less interesting at times. Constraints can breed more interesting results.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:42:00-08:00","id":43211,"title":"","content":"Okay, I quite like this.<br /> <br /> So... first of all, I agree that really, Dragonblooded have Castes. If anything, they have Castes more than Solars do - you are born and bred into a specific role<br /> <br /> .<br /> Lunars AREN'T and DON'T. They don't have powers based on &quot;job&quot;, they have powers based on &quot;aptitudes&quot;. You don't learn to be smarter, or stronger, or even more agile - you *train*, yes, but that's not something you *learn*, it's something you *become*.<br /> <br /> <br /> Arguably Aspects fits even better with the changing Casteless; they shift from having the Aspect of a Full Moon to to having the Aspect of a No Moon, etc?<br /> <br /> <br /> So one idea I like would be making Casteless (needs a new name) more than just a gimped add-on. Give them the same number of Favoured Attributes, and allow them to pick them... but if they ever pick a single Aspect, their Favoured Attributes change permanently (possibly putting them into XP debt?). That, and make the Anima Powers less specialised so a character might want to cycle through them (but otoh, might still well be annoyed that their options are changing by the moon), or alternatively forget &quot;change with the phases of the moon&quot; - have the Casteless be able to choose at will from between the three Aspects of Luna, but only get a lesser version (making them jack-of-all-trades types).<br /> <br /> Heck, while we're here, make the fixed castes something the Lunars did because they wanted the power and focus they bring. So while in the First Age a Lunar was simply defined by what they chose to work at (a Lunar was simply a Lunar, as changeable as their patron), in the time since they have reforged themselves into human weapons. Whether or not this is a homage, unconscious or not, to the lost Solar's Castes - or even to the Castes of their Dragonblooded enemies - is debatable, though Lunar Elders may well take exception to anyone suggesting this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:43:59-08:00","id":43213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43199#post43199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the critter themes aren't bad in themselves, and never really were IMHO. They could maybe be a bit more impactful or interesting though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something that the devs are obviously looking to fix this time around, along with avoiding the two mistakes of the Lunar Exalted being held up as &quot;the best shapeshifters in the world&quot; or &quot;the only real shapeshifters in the world&quot;.<br /> <br /> From the look of things, the Lunar Exalted will be boiled down to the essentials of &quot;barbaric animal-shapeshifter heroes&quot;, which is a much more concrete theme to build around. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Different for different's sake is an issue really. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> tossing something out without first seeing what can be done to make it work seems to me less interesting at times. Constraints can breed more interesting results. </div> </div> </div>The original three Castes HAVE been tried. People choosing just two Caste Attributes and adding one or two more Favored Attributes has ALSO been tried.<br /> <br /> How has that worked out?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:49:17-08:00","id":43217,"title":"","content":"By the book, you get one Attribute. As per Alchemicals, three seemed to do the job. Issues on three Castes historically is that you really can't live in your own Caste forever, so you will eventually be hitting the xp hit for non-favored stuff.<br /> <br /> There are ways around this, but I don't htink the three Castes as is is the problem. I think that as I noted, de-emphasizing Caste for Lunars entirely is probably the route to go, and the current setup we have been getting with purposeful Caste-breaking helps in doing this. Actually seeing the issue and donig more than a token post-hoc hackjob might also help. Not owrrying on Castes and utilizing totems more also helps. Codifying Lunars down to a concept besides &quot;Every sort of shapeshifter ever&quot; also helps.<br /> <br /> Right now the three Castes exist in a new context. I'm curious as to whether they can work in that context as it is now and what can be done wiht it that wans't done before.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:51:59-08:00","id":43219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43172#post43172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless you wanted to coordinate attacks or run a military apparatus, in which case Changing Moons and No Moons would be a better choice. Yes, you could conceivably pick another Attribute that could help, but that would only give you a limited in on that arena. Ask yourself, &quot;How much does it help being in charge of a military organization at some level of hierarchy to be able to vastly outpace, overpower and outlast the troops under your command?&quot;<br /> <br /> Full Moons would be dynamite special forces types or spies trusted with autonomy out in the field, but being in any position of authority which relies on the strength of others isn't playing to the Full Moon's being, whereas a Dawn could just learn War and be fine with all of the tasks that involve military organizations. This is why it's a mistake to think of Full Moons as being exactly like Dawns or filling even remotely similar roles. Additionally, those physical properties can have a lot of odd side benefits, such as using claws to climb or carve sculptures (that this option was not given is an issue of EX2's Silver Solar issue; even the poor execution of Lunars in EX1 offered a wider array of possibilities for dangerous body parts in its own fashion).</div> </div> </div> </div>You know you're making my point for me here, right? I never said Full Moons were exactly like Dawns, I said that they're pigeonholed into warriors and aren't given the tools to be anything more than that. This is a mistake from 1E onward that I hope gets corrected. By better defining the Full Moon Caste, they'd be given more freedom and would be able to do more, to be more. As 1E and 2E stand, they're written up - look not just at the Charms, but how they're described in the Traits chapter - as being warriors first, nothing else second. Dawns at least have the luxury of being defined as warriors, leaders, and tacticians. They get to be more because they get to do more. You don't have to make Full Moons more like Dawns - in fact, I'd rather they didn't - but can define them in a similar way so as to give the Caste clearer potential.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't even consider what you do. With Lunars, concentrate on what a member of each Caste is. The process will be profoundly different from Ability-based Exalted, but that's the point of the exercise. If it's that off-putting, you might not actually like Lunars. There's nothing wrong with that, but the Lunars shouldn't be bent around to be similar to other Exalted for any reason. That was done in EX2, and it didn't work out too well. </div> </div> </div>They don't have to be similar. I like that they stand out, and that's why they're my favorite Exalted. My perspective is that they've been plagued with issues since 1E because they lack the definition that the others have. I hope the Lunars remain as outstanding in concept as they've always been, but there's nothing wrong with looking at what the other Exalted get right and consider applying it to the Lunars. One thing that literally every other Exalted type has that Lunars don't is definition. The way Lunars are described, the roles they're given, and the place they have in the setting has always been broad strokes. All I'm saying is that maybe the writers should consider using the same brush they've painted the others with. Use a different palette of course, but the same level of detail in not just what Lunars are, but what they do. Maybe a paint roller ain't the way to go this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:54:39-08:00","id":43222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43170#post43170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one beef I have with organising the Lunars as Warrior/Courtier/Sage is that it makes them come across as Solars lite and just aping the Dawn/Twilight/Eclipse. Couldn't Lunars have something completely different like Brutality/Finesse/Guile or whatever, the different castes/aspects could have different means to achieve similar effects and all of them could fill the warrior/sage/courtier roles in a group but they'd do it differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why some care would be needed to show why Dawns, Battles, Dusks, Slayers (Or the 3E analog), and Full Moon are different. They all focus in the realm of the physical. In the world of War. Likewise, there are the same parallels in the social and mental arenas. To go with a Brutality, Finesse, and Guile route or more properly a Power/Finesse/Resistance route because Guile may be one form of finesse, the nWoD attributes would be optimal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1787-vince","name":"Vince","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T17:05:15-08:00","id":43230,"title":"","content":"They've already said that the original Attributes, not the NWoD ones, will be what they're using. Honestly, it's kind of better that way. Aside from the more clearly defined Presence/Manipulation dichotomy, they're not really appropriate for the setting.<br /> <br /> But let's keep it to Lunars. While Lunar discussion has sidetracked enough other threads that they'd deserve to be sidelined the same way, I'd rather not get them mad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T19:36:36-08:00","id":43290,"title":"","content":"Lunars should definitely have Castes over Aspects. I'm not even sure how this is a debate. The accumulated detritus that comes along with Aspects is certainly not going to work well for Lunars; they're iconoclasts and loners. Trying to stick them in pretty little boxes and tie them up with bows isn't going to go over well.<br /> <br /> I doubt Luna's interested in that, either. I think we just need to allow that Lunar chargen really ought to be 2 Attributes from their &quot;go to&quot; problem-solving tools, and 2 more that can go wherever it makes sense for the Lunar. If a Lunar happens to physically subdue or surmount their opponents/obstacles in the trials because it was about to attack something else/someone was going die/etc, that doesn't necessarily mean physicality is their only method. Just one that worked well in that specific instance.<br /> <br /> I don't think Luna would look for heroes that one-dimensional. I don't think you'll find many Lunars who, at 200+xp, could be considered that one-dimensional. Why should we start them out trying to fit them into orderly boxes when we know they're going to rip up the gift wrap later?<br /> <br /> If I were approaching this particular design conundrum, I'd try to design five interesting anima abilities for Lunars. I'd allow that they can &quot;align&quot; themselves to whichever one makes the most sense for them at chargen. I'd note they don't even necessarily have to keep the same one forever. The only thing they can't do is switch their favored attributes around. Totem animals can be changed when they choose a new anima (however that is accomplished). I'd probably disregard most of the remainder of their baggage; don't bring it up and let Storytellers that want those old mechanics to come back figure out their own implementations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T19:39:38-08:00","id":43291,"title":"","content":"You know, this thread would probably be more productive if we had more than one data point. Any chance we could get some Liminal spoilers?<br /> <br /> So far, I've been assuming that the major mechanical difference between Castes and Aspects is that Aspects can give one charm different effects. If that's not it, I'd like to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T19:51:01-08:00","id":43294,"title":"","content":"Aspects are not and have never been the same as Castes. <br /> <br /> So the thought that Lunars might have Aspects is a fairly progressive one, because it would change them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T19:58:54-08:00","id":43295,"title":"","content":"I can't have an opinion about this if there's no objective definition of aspect. I'm feeling silly here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T20:12:42-08:00","id":43306,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm with Gonzo. I just don't have a clear enough grasp on the distinction. Would someone on the EX3 Team be able to help elucidate, or point us in the right direction? I want to understand this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T20:21:48-08:00","id":43310,"title":"","content":"Castes and Aspects approach the causality of their talents in opposite way. <br /> <br /> You become a Dawn Caste because you have certain qualities; you have certain qualities because you are a Fire Aspect. Obviously there is nuance to this, but I feel this has a grain of truth. There is that feeling as a Dragon-Blooded that using the powers of a different Aspect is partaking of a completely different nature than your own, both in the departure from your usual aesthetics and elements and from the Essence surcharge you suffer for it.<br /> <br /> Dividing Lunars into Aspects would suggest this, to my mind - that a Lunar enters an Aspect to <i>become</i>. Rather than having elders scrutinize your life and deeds and deducing which Caste would best fit you, you choose which qualities you desire, which powers you seek. The power of the Lunar Exaltation is raw and protean, and the Aspects of the moon are ways of channeling it towards a more specific purpose, and you <i>make </i>that purpose, instead of it being an extrapolation of who you are. <br /> <br /> So, a scholar who must find the power to go at the heart of the Realm to rescue his daughter sold in slavery might ask to become a Changing Moon; it is not who he is, but it is who he needs to be. <br /> <br /> And in turn, once taken, the Aspect informs your nature and shapes you. There is a spark of lunacy in you, and its form is moulded by the Aspect you have taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T20:54:15-08:00","id":43324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43294#post43294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspects are not and have never been the same as Castes.<br /> <br /> So the thought that Lunars might have Aspects is a fairly progressive one, because it would change them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Change for changes sake isn't really being progressive...<br /> <br /> I've never seen a definition of Castes and Aspects that I can really recall, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T22:58:13-08:00","id":43363,"title":"","content":"They actually define it pretty well in the books, it seems. Blaque made an analysis of the caste/aspect difference early on in the thread and reading through the books again it seems quite accurate. And here's the descriptions as written in their respective cores.<br /> <br /> CASTE<br /> A pivotal aspect of any Exalted character is his caste.<br /> Each of the Solar Exalted is chosen by the Unconquered Sun because they embody a caste\u2019s ideals. A character\u2019s caste affects the Abilities he shows an affinity toward, the powers<br /> he develops and his role in his circle. While members of each caste are often chosen for certain traits and qualities, your individual character may break from the caste\u2019s stereotypical<br /> image. Every Dawn Caste member is a warrior, but your Dawn Caste character could be a sorcerer who excels at spells relating to combat or a general so charismatic that the sound of her voice makes enemy troops turn traitor and join her forces.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ELEMENTAL ASPECT<br /> Every Dragon-Blood belongs to one of fi ve elemental aspects that correspond to the Elemental Dragons of Air, Earth, Fire, Water and Wood. Aspect gives the character a spiritual and physical<br /> bond with that particular element, which reveals itself in her appearance, her talents and the powers she wields as a member of the Dragon-Blooded Host. <br /> Nothing impacts the life of a Terrestrial Exalt so much as the Elemental Dragon whose power she channels. Aspect plays a powerful role in determining the Exalt\u2019s temperament, aptitudes and the way she interacts with the world. Elder Terrestrials are much more prone to showing their elemental aspect through small unconscious habits than are recently Exalted Dragon-Bloods, who have not yet had the years of experience with their respective element to color their interactions with the world around them. So extreme are the differences between the elemental aspects that philosophers<br /> among the Dragon-Blooded have long asserted\u2014rhetorically, of course\u2014that the Terrestrial Exalted are not one race but fi ve, bound together by tradition, necessity and shared blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T00:01:05-08:00","id":43377,"title":"","content":"Hm, on further thoughts:<br /> <br /> <b>Castes</b> are based on your deeds: you are chosen as a Dawn because of your combat prowess or tactical acumen. The diligent study of unknown horrors has proven to the UCS that you are worthy of the title of Twilight Caste Solar.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspects </b>are more along the line of your origins: Elemental Exaltation and its Aspects are hereditery (I am not completely usre if it's something totally random, or do you still have to prove 'worthy' of it) while Liminal's Aspects are decided through the method of their 'birth'.<br /> <br /> So Caste is a reflection of who you are as a person, and the deeds to your name, while Aspect is more what you are, almost independant of who you are.<br /> <br /> <br /> For Lunas this becomes extra fun, due to 'Caste fixing'. Not sure if that will be a thing still in 3E, but the quirk of Caste fixing is that it isn't your patron who decides your Caste: it's other Lunars, who decide your Caste based on.... your aptitudes and your nature, if I understand it correctly? I can see Aspects instead of Caste if you just say that 'Aspect fixing' is not simply attaching a Caste template to your Lunar, but rather it is the refining of your essence with the being of who you are, what you are, and how you do things: a warrior who spent his life fighting could have the aspect of the Full Moon, as he views every fight as a challenge, while one who is tired of fighting would look at alternate routs, and be a No or Changing Moon instead.<br /> <br /> Though looking at that explanation, it seems Castes have more staying power. Though much hinges on Caste fixing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T01:41:08-08:00","id":43394,"title":"","content":"Personally my take would be to give DBs and Sidereals aspects while Solars and Lunars have castes. Aspects are when you only get one kind of Exalt for a particular being. Castes are when you get more than one from a single being. Luna has three different kinds of Chosen based on herself(or 4, or 5, or 6, whichever) so she has Castes. The Chosen of Endings just has one kind so she gets aspects. Hesiesh just has one kind so they are aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T01:58:06-08:00","id":43395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BogMod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43394#post43394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally my take would be to give DBs and Sidereals aspects while Solars and Lunars have castes. Aspects are when you only get one kind of Exalt for a particular being. Castes are when you get more than one from a single being. Luna has three different kinds of Chosen based on herself(or 4, or 5, or 6, whichever) so she has Castes. The Chosen of Endings just has one kind so she gets aspects. Hesiesh just has one kind so they are aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aspects of Destiny?<br /> <br /> ... That would also fit with Alchemical Exalted having Castes... But if Liminal Exalted only have a singular &quot;Dark Mother&quot;, that wouldn't fit very well as to why they have Aspects...<br /> <br /> That's an interesting thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T02:29:55-08:00","id":43405,"title":"","content":"It's difficult to talk about the Liminals like that when we know so little about their patron or their metaphysics. I seem to recall it being said somewhere that the Dark Mother wasn't their original creator but someone who had appropriated them from someone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T05:38:14-08:00","id":43457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43395#post43395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if Liminal Exalted only have a singular &quot;Dark Mother&quot;, that wouldn't fit very well as to why they have Aspects...</div> </div> </div> </div>They only have a single patron, true, but she needs the hands of others to do her work, and so her power is refracted through the lens of their passions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T06:03:00-08:00","id":43463,"title":"","content":"hmm as many have already posted the definition of a caste/aspect, im going to skip that and go onto which they should have. I do like the three types of lunar, the vagueness of &quot;warrior&quot; can leave to many different variations that can lead to interesting characters but if they were to have aspects it may be interesting as they would gain a &quot;influence&quot; of luna. this could lead to full moons being based off her full moon self, which is a rage filled bloodthirsty warrior barbarian, though I do like aspects I don't this this really benefits lunas, as there malleable natures normally requires them variety. unless lunar changes heavily to compensate the lunas wont really fit them, well that's my opinion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1215-black-orchid","name":"black orchid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1215_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T06:31:46-08:00","id":43479,"title":"","content":"My guess would be that the Liminal Exalted have Aspects because they started out as dead bodies and had Exaltations put inside them. Essentially they were &quot;born&quot; with it. This is another argument as to why Sidereals should perhaps have Aspects instead of Castes. Each Sidereal Caste is rooted to a different god, and their Exalted Essences come to them at birth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:00:07-08:00","id":43487,"title":"","content":"New point: No other splat in the game tries to ape the Solar-type Exalts by making &quot;warrior&quot; a caste or aspect. The Sidereal Castes of Battles and Endings are about facilitating battles and endings in various forms and ways, and the whole Terrestrial and Alchemical Hosts are talented warriors regardless of Aspect or Caste. Why not give the Lunars the other four Solar Castes, too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-06-2014, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:20:49-08:00","id":43493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vince</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43222#post43222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why some care would be needed to show why Dawns, Battles, Dusks, Slayers (Or the 3E analog), and Full Moon are different. They all focus in the realm of the physical. In the world of War. Likewise, there are the same parallels in the social and mental arenas. To go with a Brutality, Finesse, and Guile route or more properly a Power/Finesse/Resistance route because Guile may be one form of finesse, the nWoD attributes would be optimal.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need nWoD attributes, for instance consider<br /> Full Moon: Strength/Charisma/Perception<br /> Changing Moon: Dexterity/Manipulation/Wits<br /> New Moon: Stamina/Appearance/Intelligence<br /> <br /> Now each of them would have the flexibility to do whatever they wanted but they'd do it differently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43290#post43290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars should definitely have Castes over Aspects. I'm not even sure how this is a debate. The accumulated detritus that comes along with Aspects is certainly not going to work well for Lunars; they're iconoclasts and loners. Trying to stick them in pretty little boxes and tie them up with bows isn't going to go over well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You'll have to explain to me why you feel a Fire Aspect is in a tighter box then a Dawn Caste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:33:13-08:00","id":43500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43493#post43493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll have to explain to me why you feel a Fire Aspect is in a tighter box then a Dawn Caste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your question is equivalent to &quot;explain to me why a straight jacket is more confining than handcuffs&quot; in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:39:54-08:00","id":43508,"title":"","content":"Just to follow up, although I said I can see Lunar Aspects, I still prefer Castes, albeit with less of an idea of Lunar roles than of differing approaches to the overall Lunar nature and delineations of the Argent Madonna.<br /> <br /> Full Moons as the unstoppable fury, Changing Moons as the playful allure, No Moons as the psychedelic mystery.<br /> <br /> Note my word choice to imply those as things the Lunar <i>is</i> rather than qualities they have, which I think can also play into their transformative nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:42:06-08:00","id":43509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43324#post43324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Change for changes sake isn't really being progressive...</div> </div> </div> </div>In a subject that has been really heavily marked for a long time by focusing on things Lunars currently have and how to remove them, or remaking them from the ground up, I'd say an idea of changing Caste for Aspect is a step forward.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:52:35-08:00","id":43515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43500#post43500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your question is equivalent to &quot;explain to me why a straight jacket is more confining than handcuffs&quot; in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other people don't have the same axiomatic points. You might want to explain your animosity on that point, since we're having a discussion of all things Aspect and Caste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 01-06-2014, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T08:16:35-08:00","id":43534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43290#post43290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Trying to stick them in pretty little boxes and tie them up with bows isn't going to go over well.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?638939-Exalted-3e-Discussion-Thread-2-Atelier-Arianna&amp;p=17483173#post17483173\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...3#post17483173</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T08:35:38-08:00","id":43543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=42990#post42990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note, the devs have stated that Liminals have Aspects, not castes. I want to say that they posted a working definition of the difference at some point, but I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooof. That makes this whole description a bit difficult, because without knowing much about Liminals, we only have one example of aspects, so it's hard for us to say what makes them different.<br /> <br /> That said, the basic idea of defining Lunars differently from most other Exalted seems good, and I think that in <i>particular</i> changing the basic way they're divided up could help with the problem that we have so many exalted divided up into Fighty Class / Talky Class / Casty Class that it often feels like Lunars have nowhere to go. (Most of the other splats' castes are better-defined on those axes than Lunars are and, given that Lunars are Ability-based, they're probably better-defined that way than Lunars are ever going to be -- defining the caste that gets Strength solely as the Fighty Caste is skipping over a bunch of stuff that they should be good at; defining the caste that gets Intelligence solely as the Wizard Caste is, too.)<br /> <br /> I'd say that aspects are more defined by thematic statements about what they are rather than what they do; and that seem to be an interesting idea for Lunars. However, you'd still need interesting definitions, and (given that they only have three aspects, unless that changes, too) they'd have to be fairly broad to meaningfully cover all the attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 01-06-2014, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T08:48:43-08:00","id":43551,"title":"","content":"Did people miss my reference to John's statement on the difference between Aspect and Caste on the first page?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">without knowing much about Liminals, we only have one example of aspects, so it's hard for us to say what makes them different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I think the preview is pretty comprehensive. Possibly to the extent that it should override prior depiction of Terrestrial Aspects.<br /> <br /> ,,, Maybe, I'm actually going to reread the books to take a check at what the Aspect write-ups say; they might be less role-oriented than the wiki summaries I first read.<br /> <br /> Another thing I would think in regards to Lunar Castes is that they'd necessarily be less broad in range than Solar Castes, because Lunars are covering an archetype and thesis that is necessarily narrower than the Solars' all-encompassing arete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T09:00:11-08:00","id":43554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43551#post43551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing I would think in regards to Lunar Castes is that they'd necessarily be less broad in range than Solar Castes, because Lunars are covering an archetype and thesis that is necessarily narrower than the Solars' all-encompassing arete.</div> </div> </div> </div>While simultaneously having their Charms channeled through Attributes, giving them a more broad array of abilities for less effort. Therein lies the conundrum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T09:00:47-08:00","id":43555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43310#post43310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Castes and Aspects approach the causality of their talents in opposite way.<br /> <br /> You become a Dawn Caste because you have certain qualities; you have certain qualities because you are a Fire Aspect. Obviously there is nuance to this, but I feel this has a grain of truth. There is that feeling as a Dragon-Blooded that using the powers of a different Aspect is partaking of a completely different nature than your own, both in the departure from your usual aesthetics and elements and from the Essence surcharge you suffer for it.<br /> <br /> Dividing Lunars into Aspects would suggest this, to my mind - that a Lunar enters an Aspect to <i>become</i>. Rather than having elders scrutinize your life and deeds and deducing which Caste would best fit you, you choose which qualities you desire, which powers you seek. The power of the Lunar Exaltation is raw and protean, and the Aspects of the moon are ways of channeling it towards a more specific purpose, and you <i>make </i>that purpose, instead of it being an extrapolation of who you are.<br /> <br /> So, a scholar who must find the power to go at the heart of the Realm to rescue his daughter sold in slavery might ask to become a Changing Moon; it is not who he is, but it is who he needs to be.<br /> <br /> And in turn, once taken, the Aspect informs your nature and shapes you. There is a spark of lunacy in you, and its form is moulded by the Aspect you have taken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. Bearing in mind that I speak from the position of someone with no practical experience of how Lunars worked throughout the history of Exalted... the idea of them choosing their Castes/Aspects based not on who they are, but who they <i>need</i> to be in order to survive, protect and thrive appeals to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T09:10:15-08:00","id":43557,"title":"","content":"It's important not to 'overfix' Lunars. While the 2e fiction was lacking, and the mechanical charm design was an issue, I'm not sure many games ground to a halt because of the castes.<br /> <br /> With Lunars, I think it's crucial to remember the analogy about the baby and the bathwater. Lunar Exalted were -almost- functional in 2e. They were hobbled by some bad mechanics and terrible fiction decisions, but beyond that, it wasn't like they needed a complete overhaul top to bottom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T09:15:38-08:00","id":43559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43557#post43557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important not to 'overfix' Lunars. While the 2e fiction was lacking, and the mechanical charm design was an issue, I'm not sure many games ground to a halt because of the castes.<br /> <br /> With Lunars, I think it's crucial to remember the analogy about the baby and the bathwater. Lunar Exalted were -almost- functional in 2e. They were hobbled by some bad mechanics and terrible fiction decisions, but beyond that, it wasn't like they needed a complete overhaul top to bottom.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of my feeling too. The Lunar Castes never were well written, but it seems folks are willing to blame the Castes and the fact that Lunars in that area of mechanics never had someone actually try to write them well and we have plenty of houserules about it appears that folks do well with extra favoreds or more flexible Castes in that area.<br /> <br /> Castes just never mattered much for Lunars. I would think that the thing to keep doing is just not worry about them as much as an element and maybe make that a by-design rather than by-accident matter to them.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T09:16:38-08:00","id":43561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43557#post43557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important not to 'overfix' Lunars. While the 2e fiction was lacking, and the mechanical charm design was an issue, I'm not sure many games ground to a halt because of the castes.<br /> <br /> With Lunars, I think it's crucial to remember the analogy about the baby and the bathwater. Lunar Exalted were -almost- functional in 2e. They were hobbled by some bad mechanics and terrible fiction decisions, but beyond that, it wasn't like they needed a complete overhaul top to bottom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, this near-acceptability was only had by copying various features of other Exalted. There wasn't a unique play experience to be had out of Lunars, so you'd have to go further back from the 2e tree to let one grow up on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T09:36:48-08:00","id":43567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43557#post43557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important not to 'overfix' Lunars. While the 2e fiction was lacking, and the mechanical charm design was an issue, I'm not sure many games ground to a halt because of the castes.<br /> <br /> With Lunars, I think it's crucial to remember the analogy about the baby and the bathwater. Lunar Exalted were -almost- functional in 2e. They were hobbled by some bad mechanics and terrible fiction decisions, but beyond that, it wasn't like they needed a complete overhaul top to bottom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I found it to be the other way around with Lunars. Their mechanics worked just fine, the prereqs might have been harsh but all the charms did what they were supposed to do unlike Sidereals or Dragonblooded. The problem with Lunars was that they were completely incoherent, the entire splat was this chimera abomination spawned from a primal soup of random cool looking themes and powers.<br /> <br /> The reason that Lunars never got any errata was that they can't be fixed by some minor changes, they do need the complete total overhaul and to make them a coherent splat a lot of things do have to be thrown out the window. I'm not sure if castes are one of those things but it's worth investigating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 01-06-2014, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T10:00:36-08:00","id":43583,"title":"","content":"Castes/aspects/etc. serve two main purposes. First and most importantly, they\u2019re there to give structure to an Exalt type to make them more interesting to the player and to facilitate character creation. Second, they\u2019re useful shorthand to describe characters: knowing that you\u2019re up against \u201ca Dawn and a Twilight\u201d is a lot more evocative and informative than \u201ctwo Solars\u201d. When you\u2019re discussing how to divide Lunars, your priorities should be into making them as interesting and easy to parse as possible.<br /> <br /> I could write an entire essay on why Lunar Castes are shit, but I\u2019ll be brief and boil it down to three things: they\u2019re overly restrictive, they\u2019re unclear, and there\u2019s too few of them. Let\u2019s hit the points one by one.<br /> <br /> First off, remember that the main purpose of a Caste/Aspect/Whatever is to provide a structure that\u2019s evocative and makes creating the character you want easier. What the Caste provides is a skeleton that you build around: it\u2019s the marrow, not the meat of what you are. For Solars, a player who is into all of his Caste Stuff and defines himself narrowly according to it is very unusual: the Castes are designed to be used so that you create \u201ca Zenith leader <i>who is also a master swordsman and has an abiding interest in finding and translating old texts\u201d</i> or \u201ca Twilight craftsman <i>who uses clever gadgets to hunt and kill the minions of Malfeas in Chiaroscuro\u201d</i>. The Caste is not who you are or what you do. The Caste is about you having a core aptitude for a certain number of things that you can raise to 5 immediately and learn cool Charms for.<br /> Lunar Castes are a straightjacket. They lock you very firmly into a McCombo package of Attributes with redundant competencies that say very firmly \u201cyou are physical/mental/social-focused\u201d. The inability to raise Attributes instantly (as Solars do with Abilities) and the high cost of raising them, the higher cost of unfavored Charms (everything outside your narrow Caste McCombo), and the fact that the system encourages specialization means that players are punished very harshly for stepping beyond the archetype\u2014for making your character interesting! The 3 Caste / 1 Favored spread is one of the dumbest things in Lunars.<br /> <br /> Second, Lunar Castes are simultaneously about Attribute lines (Physical/Social/Mental) and about roles (Warrior/Trickster/Shaman). Physical/Social/Mental as the basis of Castes is crap, because it\u2019s about as evocative as an engineering manual. Other than surface symmetry (which should never be your main design criteria) there are no good reasons whatsoever to associate Lunar archetypes to the Attribute lines. Any reworking of Castes should address this as a priority.<br /> Warrior/Trickster/Shaman is better, but still problematic. \u2018Warrior\u2019 on its own is not good enough: it\u2019s too generic and stale (fun exercise: picture the Solar Castes being called Warrior/Priest/Wizard/Rogue/Bard). From a systems design standpoint it\u2019s also a problem: for a game that is as heavily combat-centric as Exalted (compare the pagecount devoted to combat v. that for any other system aspect), presenting one of the options as the superior combat option is a mistake. The fact that a Twilight (Scholar) can match the Dawn (General) in combat is an important feature. \u2018Shaman\u2019 is also weird\u2014what is it that they do, again? Commune with nature and pray to spirits? Is this kind of thing even in their Charmset? Is there any Lunar that shows what it means to be a Shaman anywhere in the Exalted line?<br /> <br /> Third, three base archetypes is too little. Other than sticking to Attribute lines for surface symmetry, which I\u2019ve already condemned as stupid, there\u2019s no reason to limit Lunars to three castes. Alchemicals, which are also Attribute-based, get six and are the better for it. Most other Exalted types get five, which affords players a much greater variety in terms of what kind of Caste (skeleton) they want to build their characters around. Whether we go for Castes (e.g., \u2018Hunter\u2019, \u2018Trickster\u2019, \u2018Leader\u2019, \u2018Spy\u2019) or Aspects (this would be a hell of a lot easier if Lunars didn\u2019t have a personal animal totem), three archetypes isn\u2019t enough to cover the spectrum of cool characters you can build using the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","name":"Black Paper Moon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar937_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T10:16:21-08:00","id":43593,"title":"","content":"I was under the assumption that the Terrestrials were called Aspects because they were descended/empowered from different 'aspects' of Gaia (i.e. the Elemental Dragons). I'd never give it much thought beyond that other than it made them different from the Celestial Exalts. Upon greater reflection, the terms aspect, in relation to the Terrestrials, conjures, to me, a part of a greater whole. This is very much the theme of the Terrestrials, that while individually powerful, together they are truly mighty. The Lunars, on the other hand, come from one, albeit many faceted, goddess and are individually mighty.<br /> <br /> As for the names of whatever you want to use to subdivide the Lunar Exalted, I don't feel particularly strong one way or the other about referring to them as having castes or aspects. Although it does seem like 'change just for change's sake' to be honest (Which I really, really, really hope 3E is not rampant with).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Map of Third Edition Creation in a First Edition Style<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2F18ttip13xdsc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3D35f3d332551385032587cde8b093e4923ed687ee\" target=\"_blank\">\u200b</a>, (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fpjil7fcr0esc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3Dcfdff833d8e8afe3e86ca27c06569cad0bb44be9\" target=\"_blank\">3E Locations Only</a>) (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fik6dit8lrlrc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3D0e0c488dea6e066af00d52c6d5994592bb4d8359\" target=\"_blank\">1E, 2E, 3E Amalgam</a>)\u200b<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/kashi85\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt, where I post some Exalted stuffs.</a>","edited":{"userid":853,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/853-kashi","user":"Kashi","date":". 01-06-2014, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/853-kashi","name":"Kashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar853_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T10:29:52-08:00","id":43598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43543#post43543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...] without knowing much about Liminals, we only have one example of aspects, so it's hard for us to say what makes them different.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43551#post43551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, I think the preview is pretty comprehensive. Possibly to the extent that it should override prior depiction of Terrestrial Aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>For instance, the Liminal preview does not make explicit what Aspects are, but it does state what they are <i>not</i>: &quot;The Liminal Exalted lack the purpose-based Castes of the Celestial Exalted. Instead they are divided into Aspects, somewhat like the Dragon-Blooded.&quot;<br /> It then goes on to present the five Aspects in terms of the drives that spawn them, the symbolism of their names, and their behavourial tendencies; there is absolutely nothing in there about what they do or are supposed to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T10:38:56-08:00","id":43602,"title":"","content":"I'll throw in my two cents.<br /> <br /> For Lunars, I propose &quot;Phases&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T11:58:58-08:00","id":43642,"title":"","content":"All, Just my two cents, and a quickly thought out idea, but I figure that it might be an interesting idea to discuss nonetheless. What effect would modeling the Lunar Exaltation more on the attributes have? Specifically, during character gen. we have to choose an attribute spread that's favors one attribute type (Physical/Social/Mental), is a pretty even spread to the other, and handicaps the unfavored attribute type. Why not model Lunars on this? e.g. - Your Caste is your star attribute type (whether or not the abilities are reworked for the castes is immaterial and irrelevant), you then either pick a second Caste or three different attributes as your so-so attribute type, and then the last three are your unfavored. The crunch effect of this would be (potentially) XP cost and training times. So, a Full Moon (Physical) Lunar that favors the Changing Moon would pay 8 for Physical Attribute based charms, 9 for Social Attribute based charms, and 10 for Mental Attribute charms (Or 8/10/12, 6/10/14 or whatever normalizes the XP curve) and the training time could be Days/Weeks/Months (or some other calculation) to reinforce the attribute based nature of Lunars, while encouraging out-of-caste Charm purchases, but maintaining a focus on the initial attribute focus of the caste. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1932-advoicate","name":"advoicate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T12:36:52-08:00","id":43659,"title":"","content":"Theme is a factor of fiction, really ; the botch on Lunar fiction muddled thematic connotations a bit. Without a clear unifying Ubermyth to hang character traits off of, developers for Lunar Exalted sometimes would borrow Werewolfisms or other such things. I believe a fiction pass should fix this issue; we're getting that, so, I'm not worried about it. Ultimately, the 'Animal Man' myth is sufficiently deep and well represented enough so that it shouldn't be an issue.<br /> <br /> As for borrowing powers... as I've said elsewhere, so what? Yes, cool and distinctive powers are interesting, but when you really get down to it?... the Monkey King -is- kinda a silver Solar. It's just another flavor of martial arts superhuman. Some crossover is gonna exist. It's not the end of the world.<br /> <br /> The purpose is to make Lunars fun to play and to make them fit in well, which doesn't require every aspect of what Lunars are to be completely NEW, TURBO, HYPER, EXCITING and unique.<br /> <br /> It pretty much worked before ; I played many games with them, so did many others, we had then on our MUSH for many years.<br /> <br /> My impression has always been 'Lunars could be improved and need love' rather than 'Lunars are a hopeless mess of trash'.<br /> <br /> So when I say be wary of overfixing, that's what I mean. We're tinkering here, really -- doing a big fiction pass, a mechanics pass, and then we ought to be more or less ready to go. No need to make a mountain out of a molehill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T12:54:14-08:00","id":43673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43659#post43659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for borrowing powers... as I've said elsewhere, so what? Yes, cool and distinctive powers are interesting, but when you really get down to it?... the Monkey King -is- kinda a silver Solar. It's just another flavor of martial arts superhuman. Some crossover is gonna exist. It's not the end of the world.<br /> <br /> The purpose is to make Lunars fun to play and to make them fit in well, which doesn't require every aspect of what Lunars are to be completely NEW, TURBO, HYPER, EXCITING and unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly sure that noone has ever written that Lunars need their every power to be super unique. I think its worthwhile to note that Dragonblooded are not being called Scarlet Solars nor are Sidereals called Ninja Solars although both of them also have a fair bit of overlap with the Solar powerset.The first thing that makes the Lunars different from the Dragonblooded and Sidereals in this respect is that a number of Lunar charms weren't just similar, they were practically word for word copies. The second thing and the most relevant thing when it comes to discussing Lunar castes, is that the DB's and Sids do not have 1:1 analogues to Solar castes and this is hurting the Lunars really badly.<br /> <br /> A Chosen of Battles is never expected to be measured up against a Dawn and be judged as worse in every measurable way because what the Battles does is something completely different however a player can very reasonably ask &quot;Why in the world would I want have a No Moon in the group if I could have a Twilight?&quot; and the answer is &quot;You don't&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43659#post43659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It pretty much worked before ; I played many games with them, so did many others, we had then on our MUSH for many years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars have traditionally been very popular, usually the second most common splat after Solars. However that's pretty much despite their mechanics and thematics then because of it. In my experience most Lunar players really really enjoy Shapeshifting, there's so many fun things you can do with it, they also tend to enjoy the barbarian aesthetics and the whole shamanistic/animist vibe either by embracing it or deliberately playing against stereotype.<br /> <br /> That said whenever they try to do anything beyond the basic shape-shifting shenanigans and get into any kind of power contest where a Solar-equivalent is involved they quickly become frustrated over how limited they actually are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 01-06-2014, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T12:59:58-08:00","id":43674,"title":"","content":"All this discussion made me review the various aspects of Luna to see if there was anything to be gained from them. I don't think we need to go as far as having a &quot;Bloody Huntress Aspect&quot; or some-such, largely for the reasons Maddy stated above, but a few interesting ideas came out of it that I would like to share.<br /> <br /> Each of Luna's Aspects is influenced both by one of the &quot;alternate-moons&quot; and by Luna's relationship with that alternate. Thus an Aspect related to that may be based on the Exalt's relationship with Luna herself, (or perhaps with Gaia, or their Solar mate, or whatever) and that would form the basis for their powers in some way. Rather than the Solar charms which reach a pinnacle that brushes against the Unconquered Sun, Lunar charms would spring from their relationship with their patron and lead to what such emotions might push them towards.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Random thoughts that may or may not be useful.<br /> <br /> PS: Aspects of Luna notes here: <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:luna-s-aspects\" target=\"_blank\">http://nobilis.me/quotes:luna-s-aspects</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/242-mindworm-jim","name":"Mindworm Jim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T13:38:25-08:00","id":43702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43598#post43598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, the Liminal preview does not make explicit what Aspects are, but it does state what they are <i>not</i>: &quot;The Liminal Exalted lack the purpose-based Castes of the Celestial Exalted. Instead they are divided into Aspects, somewhat like the Dragon-Blooded.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If Castes are based on purpose, then the six Alchemical Castes only barely qualify (and still might be more accurately labeled Aspects) and the traditional three Lunar Castes don't qualify at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd ask why the Lunar Castes aren't more like the Alchemical Castes, but I still keep running into the issue that the Alchemical Exalted don't have <i>anything </i>like Totems, and no one else does either. The only splat that <i>did </i>were the Devil Tigers, and <i>those </i>guys got to design their own Castes, based entirely on the &quot;Totem&quot; they created through &quot;Triumphant Howl of the Devil Tiger&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I absolutely do not want Lunar Aspects based on the &quot;Other Moons&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-06-2014, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T13:42:05-08:00","id":43705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43294#post43294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspects are not and have never been the same as Castes.<br /> <br /> So the thought that Lunars might have Aspects is a fairly progressive one, because it would change them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, to get the kind of useful discussion that you seek from this thread, we may need to know how you, personally, define Aspects as opposed to Castes.<br /> <br /> We can make guesses and inferences about these terms that you would like us to discuss, but they are just that: guesses and inferences.<br /> <br /> Could you favor us with definitions, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/240-winged-cat","name":"Winged Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar240_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:22:41-08:00","id":43856,"title":"","content":"If the aspect is supposed to be defined as a the place of your power's origin, it could also be called &quot;auspice&quot; if only to trail back to old Werewolf terminology.<br /> It is a word that implies a patronage (from Luna) but also a omen regarding your role in Creation. This aspect/auspice could be shifting as long as the Lunar's essence is &quot;unbound&quot; and once you get tattooed, you're getting some more insight in what Luna has given you.<br /> Any aspects would also have to be much looser in what they define for you. Maybe a fixed favoured attribute, and the rest are up to you, due to the protean nature of the Lunar essence. It would serve them well by being the most flexible of Exalts, in terms of variations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43702#post43702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I absolutely do not want Lunar Aspects based on the &quot;Other Moons&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never really knew what those things were before reading the link further up on the thread. And I totally agree.<br /> That on the other hand, could be a cool source of more advanced charm sets for the Lunars, as the &quot;Other Moons&quot; have been consumed, and have probably left a mark on Luna and her essence.<br /> Quite fittingly, Lunar should be able to reach into these and draw some of this forgotten power to them. Maybe as a source of power for a bit more advanced characters?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T20:06:15-08:00","id":43909,"title":"","content":"WTA had splats that didn't have auspices, at least as far as the splat was named, though. Ratkin and Ananasi, among others,had aspects, though the former had a set of rather role-related ones. The latter, though, had Aspects that determined which Triatic facet that the werespider took. And after their change, these Aspects produced a series of tattoo-like patterns on them, with the design of said pattern depending on which of the three they got tapped for. The markings became more elaborate as they gained Rank, too. The Ratkin's Freak Aspects also took that kind of tack, after a fashion, since what you had was explicitly &quot;One who uses technology against itself&quot;, &quot;epidemic provocateur&quot;, &quot;delusional liar&quot;, and &quot;literally explosive rage monster&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T06:19:03-08:00","id":44119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Originally posted by hatewheel<br /> Aspect suggests a physical association, where Caste only suggests a predilection for certain kinds of action. It can be more complex than this, but this answer is the simplest version. </div> </div> </div>Reposting this from Isator Levi, upthread - this was John's simplified definition of caste versus aspect.<br /> <br /> Given that there is also an intent to make Lunars more physical in their approach to things, I can see why the novelty of exploring caste vs. aspect would be interesting.<br /> <br /> I like Omicron's idea that Lunar's choose their aspect to become something, and then it empowers them going forward - it both merges the inherent properties associated with the Aspect with the flexibility and freedom that is still part of Luna.<br /> <br /> To Sunder's idea about using totems as a jumping off point, it is actually tricky, mostly because of adjectives. For example, if my totem is Wolf, I probably am Full Moon, under your schema, right? But my concept of wolf is actually the wolf from O-kami, who is the goddess responsible for healing the world through knowledge and exploration - so maybe the adjective I need for my totem is <i>Mystic</i> Wolf, and now that totem makes me a No-Moon. Or if I apply <i>Charming</i>, it becomes a Changing Moon, etc. In the same way, a Bull is an herbivore, but I can bull examples where it is appropriate for all three extant castes. Totems are too subjective, and frankly too wide-open, to serve the sort of role that game-designers use Castes/Aspects/Auspices/Clans/Classes/Traditions/Kiths/Whatever to fill. Though, I welcome John et al. to include a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kakapo\" target=\"_blank\">kakapo</a>-totemed Lunar somewhere in Creation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I am deeply ambivalent about whether Lunars should have Castes or Aspects - given that I feel one of the defining features of Celestial Exalts in past editions has been that they transcend the limitations they find imposed upon them, I would be reluctant to give them something else as a limiter. However, I have not actually felt that Terrestrial Aspects were particularly constraining - and I note many people felt that there was no functional difference between caste and aspect.<br /> <br /> Using John's definition, I am not sure that the current Caste scheme does not mechanically have the same force as Aspects - a Full Moon has almost no way to use her 1 favored attribute to sufficiently break out of her defined role, unlike a Dawn, who could be a Sailing-Sorcerer-Diplomatic-Scholarly-Street Musician, who reluctantly is the greatest warrior alive.<br /> <br /> In this case, Caste/Favored Ability mechanics, coupled with out-of-caste point costs and even some of the Lunar societal fluff (for example, No-Moons not teaching other castes Celestial Circle Sorcery has cropped up in both editions) has also made it so that the Lunar bins are less 'predilections' and are more hard-coded...<br /> <br /> So, if we keep the current paradigm, perhaps reformatting to Aspects would give the Lunar structure the conceptual weight it needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T07:19:47-08:00","id":44148,"title":"","content":"As I note in my previous post, the current Lunar paradigm does not really function mechanically like a Caste, where it provides a predilection which can be over-ruled through the use of Favored Attributes (in this case). I previously suggest that redefining the bins as Aspects, perhaps along the lines Omicron proposed, or something equally cool, would add a conceptual weight to the tight fit that binning currently gives Lunars.<br /> <br /> The alternative is to keep Castes for Lunars, which would necessitate reworking the mechanics of the Caste/Favored framework to allow for the flexibility Castes are supposed to provide. Thus, a &quot;Full-Moon&quot; should have an inclination toward physical stuff, but should be able to sort of nod in its general direction while grabbing goodies from elsewhere.<br /> <br /> This has not happened before because of a concern over the breadth covered by the Attributes - that somehow favoring 1 Attribute (other than Dexterity) was equal to favoring 3-4 Abilities. Or maybe it is that Favoring Dexterity is equal to favoring at least 8 Abilities*, and therefore everything else gets thrown out of proportion. While the base mechanic may make that true, the result still seemed to be a less flexible character - perhaps because of how the charm trees evolved, with inconsistent requirements within a tree (switching from Charisma to Manipulation to Appearance, in 1e; in 2e it was more the huge jumps in Essence minimums, and the narrow purviews of some of the shrubs).<br /> <br /> The final challenge is that, even with a Caste/Favored discount, raising an Attribute is much more expensive that raising an Ability, and so progress feels slower, and it is harder to meet new requirements via in-game advancement. Thus, you have a strong incentive to stick to a narrow range of proficiency - which is again more in keeping with the feel of an Aspect than a Caste.<br /> <br /> *Archery, Athletics, Craft (Air), Dodge, Larceny, Martial Arts, Melee, Stealth, Thrown","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T07:57:15-08:00","id":44166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joshua</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44119#post44119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To Sunder's idea about using totems as a jumping off point, it is actually tricky, mostly because of adjectives. For example, if my totem is Wolf, I probably am Full Moon, under your schema, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely not.<br /> <br /> By my proposal, &quot;Wolf&quot; would have nothing to do with any Caste or Aspect. Those are determined (or made redundant) by the brush you use to paint &quot;Wolf&quot;. For example, &quot;All-Devouring Fenris-Wolf&quot; is very different from &quot;Wise Wolf Among the Wheat and Spices&quot;.<br /> <br /> Both may have a simple wolf form for their spirit shape, depending on how spirit shapes work... but the personal embellishments to &quot;Wolf&quot; give rise to their four Totemic (favored) Attributes and any further Totemic keywords.<br /> <br /> The player who chooses to be a wolf that is wise and concerned with agricultural success and economics is creating a Totem which resonates with Intelligence, Perception, Charisma and Manipulation (her Totemic Attributes) as much as Fenrisulfr resonates with the physical Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":".  stupid iphone doesn't include page-spaces, stupid wesbite 01-07-2014, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T07:58:28-08:00","id":44167,"title":"","content":"I'll agree that based on Hatewheels description the current Lunar divisions (Physical/Social/Mental) make a ton more sense as Aspects then Castes as it's hard to get more defined by your physical attributes then that. Sure the Full Moon isn't forced to have physical as his primary but if he doesn't he'll just suck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joshua</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44119#post44119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> However, I have not actually felt that Terrestrial Aspects were particularly constraining - and I note many people felt that there was no functional difference between caste and aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no mechanically defined differences between castes and aspects. The Dragonblooded have more mechanics that interact with their aspect then the other Exalts do with their castes but there's no way to say if that's a DB mechanic or Aspect mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 01-07-2014, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T08:36:28-08:00","id":44186,"title":"","content":"I am under the impression that the hard division in Attribute + Ability for all situations is going away. Realistically, most of the time Stealth and Larceny should probably be rolled with Wits and not Dexterity. Melee with Strength. Etcetera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44167#post44167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll agree that based on Hatewheels description the current Lunar divisions (Physical/Social/Mental) make a ton more sense as Aspects then Castes as it's hard to get more defined by your physical attributes then that. Sure the Full Moon isn't forced to have physical as his primary but if he doesn't he'll just suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are we insisting that Lunars favor an entire Attribute category? We already know that wasn't the original intention and it certainly works worse than the original intention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T08:44:28-08:00","id":44192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44186#post44186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am under the impression that the hard division in Attribute + Ability for all situations is going away. Realistically, most of the time Stealth and Larceny should probably be rolled with Wits and not Dexterity. Melee with Strength. Etcetera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where'd you get this impression?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44186#post44186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are we insisting that Lunars favor an entire Attribute category? We already know that wasn't the original intention and it certainly works worse than the original intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars were originally split in those Attribute categories, hence three Castes. We weren't really ever supposed to get around to describing the lost ones and how they fit into the Attribute setup. That it hasn't worked as-written was the poor implementation of Luanrs 1e and the lazy or reactionary implementation of aspects of Lunars in 2e.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T08:49:30-08:00","id":44197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44186#post44186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are we insisting that Lunars favor an entire Attribute category? We already know that wasn't the original intention and it certainly works worse than the original intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> The current three Castes would be much improved by returning to the original Second Edition intent that you favor only two Caste Attributes and get to pick any other two Attributes. While you generally want at least a Charm from each of your Caste's three associated Attributes, it's the rare character concept that will lead to have a dozen Charms from each of the three. If you only want a few Stamina Charms, your Full Moon doesn't need to favor Stamina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:14:53-08:00","id":44222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44186#post44186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are we insisting that Lunars favor an entire Attribute category? We already know that wasn't the original intention and it certainly works worse than the original intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing original about Peter Schaefers chargen, back in first edition Lunars didn't even have favoured attributes at all, they had their caste attributes and that was it. I'm all for changing it but as things are aspect certainly sounds fitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:15:18-08:00","id":44223,"title":"","content":"You could also jus let Lunars favor two Attributes beyond their Caste, which seems less fiddly to me.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:17:21-08:00","id":44225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44197#post44197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While you generally want at least a Charm from each of your Caste's three associated Attributes, it's the rare character concept that will lead to have a dozen Charms from each of the three. If you only want a few Stamina Charms, your Full Moon doesn't need to favor Stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Full Moon characters want charms from all three attributes all the time but that's probably because the physical trees are the only ones designed with the slightest bit of synergy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:21:21-08:00","id":44229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44223#post44223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also jus let Lunars favor two Attributes beyond their Caste, which seems less fiddly to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leaving that aside, we'd still have the problem that the Full Moons are painted as warriors instead of athletes. Not that I <i>want </i>them painted as athletes, per se, but all Lunar Exalted are warriors if all Dragon-Blooded or Alchemicals are warriors.<br /> <br /> This isn't a mechanical problem at all, since the Full Moon anima power works just great for any Full Moon concept, whether peaceful laborer, far-ranging traveling, or proud athletic competitor. It's just a fiction problem that places undue expectations on Full Moons and pulls those expectations away from Lunars of other Castes (or Aspects).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:30:23-08:00","id":44235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44192#post44192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where'd you get this impression?<br /> <br /> Lunars were originally split in those Attribute categories, hence three Castes. We weren't really ever supposed to get around to describing the lost ones and how they fit into the Attribute setup. That it hasn't worked as-written was the poor implementation of Luanrs 1e and the lazy or reactionary implementation of aspects of Lunars in 2e.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the way the hard divisions were specifically called out as a problem. How they've been removed in every single OPP game published since. Little hints like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44222#post44222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing original about Peter Schaefers chargen, back in first edition Lunars didn't even have favoured attributes at all, they had their caste attributes and that was it. I'm all for changing it but as things are aspect certainly sounds fitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Schaefer said that his system was the one that went with his draft and it got edited to what it currently is after that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:35:12-08:00","id":44238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44229#post44229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Leaving that aside, we'd still have the problem that the Full Moons are painted as warriors instead of athletes. Not that I <i>want </i>them painted as athletes, per se, but all Lunar Exalted are warriors if all Dragon-Blooded or Alchemicals are warriors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be unimaginative but I see only two ways to achieve that goal.<br /> Alternative A: Rearrange the attributes into a setup that doesn't represent warrior/priest/mage.<br /> Alternative B: Make it so that all attributes are competitive in combat<br /> <br /> If you look at the Dragon-blooded they do a little bit of both, a lot of abilities that you'd think are non-combat contains combat charms and all their aspects have some dedicated combat ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 01-07-2014, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:47:39-08:00","id":44247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44197#post44197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The current three Castes would be much improved by returning to the original Second Edition intent that you favor only two Caste Attributes and get to pick any other two Attributes. While you generally want at least a Charm from each of your Caste's three associated Attributes, it's the rare character concept that will lead to have a dozen Charms from each of the three. If you only want a few Stamina Charms, your Full Moon doesn't need to favor Stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the goal is to reinforce the Caste, it's better to do like Solars and give them 3 out of 4 or 5 Caste Attributes and using the expanded spread to give the Castes an actual function. Reducing the Caste Attributes just reinforces the idea that Castes aren't important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T10:06:43-08:00","id":44260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44247#post44247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the goal is to reinforce the Caste, it's better to do like Solars and give them 3 out of 4 or 5 Caste Attributes and using the expanded spread to give the Castes an actual function.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attributes are not Abilities. What works for Ability-based Castes will not work for Attribute-based Castes.<br /> <br /> Besides which, what are the options? Full Moons can make use of Charisma training-and-command Charms, Manipulation tricks-and-feints Charms, Appearance stealth Charms, Perception Charms, Wits Charms, and Intelligence-based Sorcery. All of the attributes can apply to War!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reducing the Caste Attributes just reinforces the idea that Castes aren't important. </div> </div> </div>Compared to the Totem, they're not.<br /> <br /> Again, note that by &quot;Totem&quot; I mean &quot;the iconic image of the basic animal with the embellishments of favored Attributes&quot;. Not &quot;wolf&quot;, but &quot;Wise Wolf Horo&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T10:19:06-08:00","id":44264,"title":"","content":"I would also be down for somehow incorporating the Totem into the Castes somehow. There are several animal archetypes (Predator, Scavenger, Migrator, Builder, Herd/Pack Animal) that could work as Castes/Aspects. Castes to Lunars have never felt like nearly as important a part of their character than their totem. With the other Exalted, one's Caste/Aspect is a defining trait. With Lunars, it feels like little more than a limitation placed on them. Maybe finding a way to amalgamate the two is the way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:11:37-08:00","id":44301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44238#post44238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might be unimaginative but I see only two ways to achieve that goal.<br /> Alternative A: Rearrange the attributes into a setup that doesn't represent warrior/priest/mage.<br /> Alternative B: Make it so that all attributes are competitive in combat<br /> <br /> If you look at the Dragon-blooded they do a little bit of both, a lot of abilities that you'd think are non-combat contains combat charms and all their aspects have some dedicated combat ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Marathon running* is technically non-combat, as is withstanding the elements or many applications of producing poison or diseases (court intrigue, strategic denial of wells, etc.)<br /> <br /> All of the setup for Physical Attributes to apply to non-combat situations exist, but the amount of attention that they've had has been historically low in favor of many different iterations of Weak Version of Solar Combat Charm and On-Strength Version of Solar Combat Charm With Drastically Reduced Duration. We were starting to see social applications for Strength back in would-be errata teased way, way back, such as Scar-Making Blow being used to produce Emotion-type influences based on how the Lunar handed out the scars, and it was promising. You could probably still do social stuff based on Physical Attributes with shapeshifting, too. People crave and admire power, so being a physical powerhouse should have some bearing on influencing others.<br /> <br /> *Useful for being a messenger, or in other words, doing something that the Eclipse Caste usually does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T13:08:07-08:00","id":44382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44301#post44301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Marathon running* is technically non-combat, as is withstanding the elements or many applications of producing poison or diseases (court intrigue, strategic denial of wells, etc.)<br /> <br /> All of the setup for Physical Attributes to apply to non-combat situations exist, but the amount of attention that they've had has been historically low in favor of many different iterations of Weak Version of Solar Combat Charm and On-Strength Version of Solar Combat Charm With Drastically Reduced Duration. We were starting to see social applications for Strength back in would-be errata teased way, way back, such as Scar-Making Blow being used to produce Emotion-type influences based on how the Lunar handed out the scars, and it was promising. You could probably still do social stuff based on Physical Attributes with shapeshifting, too. People crave and admire power, so being a physical powerhouse should have some bearing on influencing others.<br /> <br /> *Useful for being a messenger, or in other words, doing something that the Eclipse Caste usually does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this approach would be really interesting - and incline toward an Aspect rather than a Caste. Here, you see the nature of the Aspect permeating every component of the character's nature. <br /> <br /> Exploring it further, while keeping the 3 original bins for purposes of changing as little as possible per experiment:<br /> Changing Moon: Combat charms using deception and/or taunts to control combat momentum; social charms as before-ish, but more Lunar; learning charms based on interrogating things/people, stuff like that?<br /> No Moons: Combat charms using advanced tactics and heightened perception - like that Hugh Jackman Sherlock Holmes movie sequence; Social charms involving analysis of tells and ticks; mental things related to mental things?<br /> <br /> As a note, the above are not in any way intended to be exclusive. I recognize that I left out non-combat physical charms - mostly because I am terrible at ideas for those sorts of things, and rather than mess around, I am just letting it alone, and leaving it to someone more talented than I am.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T13:46:23-08:00","id":44413,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, Lunar Castes are not about <b>What</b> a Lunar does, so much as <b>How</b>.<br /> <br /> A Full Moon can be a thief without anything remotely resembling morals, or an honourable war-lord, or a pacifist monk - but all three rely on their physical abilities to achieve their goals, whether they sneak about unannounced, single-handedly smite the enemy's army, or wander without food or rest for weeks at a time.<br /> <br /> A Changing Moon can be an honest trader, a passionate storyteller, or a heartless courtier... But they all rely on their social skills, whether they rely on truth and honesty, a talent for playing other's minds and feelings, or raw force of personality.<br /> <br /> A No Moon can be a keeper of secrets and forbidden lore, a master of courtly intrigue, or a radical thinker and reformist; either way, whether they rely on their memory and deductive reasoning, attention to detail and pattern recognition, or their quick thinking and sharp tongue, they are all about mental prowess.<br /> <br /> I suppose this makes them more suited as Aspects than Castes, but I don't really think it makes that much of a difference - certainly, there are more important details to worry about (cough-Tell-cough).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T13:54:21-08:00","id":44421,"title":"","content":"I never got the point of &quot;Castes&quot; versus &quot;Aspects.&quot; It always seemed a semantics thing in the first place, like the Dragonbloods took to calling themselves that to set them apart from the &quot;Anathema.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T17:09:20-08:00","id":44554,"title":"","content":"An Aspect connotes very little beyond an<i> idea </i>of what you will be like. Aspects imply things about demeanor, appearance, and (often latent) skills. They also demonstrate the nature of your power, such that it is essentially different from that of another Aspect. It has almost nothing to do with your expected role. A Fire Aspect is not guaranteed to be a fighter. He might be a socialite. Aspect says so little about the differences in Dragon-Blooded that you can expect similar roles from all of them. They are inherently soldiers, inherently group-arrayed, and inherently familial.<br /> <br /> Castes say a lot more. Castes are fixed. You do not fall out of Castes. It is not expected that a Dawn will be something other than a fighter. Castes align with the person you were before Exaltation. Characters can deviate from Castes, but it is very rare that they simply cease to operate within their definitions. Meanwhile, Dragon-Blooded are not deliberately Chosen for their skills and talents. They are an outgrowth of their parents' (and their parents') Aspects, and so they inherit blood traits, and those are expressed when they come into their own Aspects. Denying an Aspect is not essentially possible because Aspects intermingle in the blood, just as traits of the parents mingle to create children. Dragon-Blooded have flex. Solars do not. They are not inheriting anything so much as they are exemplifying who they always were to begin with. Castes are an extremely strong predictor for roles and social placement as only persons who would fit those roles are Chosen in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T17:36:00-08:00","id":44570,"title":"","content":"That to me raises the question, if Lunars had aspects, how would their aspect be determined? Would it be based on where/when they Exalted? Would Luna pick it for them? Would it be inherited from whichever Lunar gave them their tattoos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T17:46:09-08:00","id":44575,"title":"","content":"Something about their personality calls out to Luna and she Exalts them. Aggression and resilience gets Full Moon, deceitfulness and cunning get Changing Moon, patience and wisdom get No Moon, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T18:12:49-08:00","id":44583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44570#post44570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That to me raises the question, if Lunars had aspects, how would their aspect be determined? Would it be based on where/when they Exalted? Would Luna pick it for them? Would it be inherited from whichever Lunar gave them their tattoos?</div> </div> </div> </div> Based on John's definitions, if Lunars had Aspects, the Tattoos would seem like a good source, because those are decided by another Lunar rather than by the Exaltation. But it seems like a better idea to have Castes than Aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T18:18:12-08:00","id":44589,"title":"","content":"When an Alchemical is made, their Caste is chosen based on the nature of their past lives, and their personality reflects those past lives, and thus their Chosen Caste. It is probably because of this deliberate design that Alchemicals do not have Aspects. Liminals get Aspects because of the accidental nature of their birth, in becoming something their creators did not intend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T18:22:01-08:00","id":44590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44554#post44554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Aspect connotes very little beyond an<i> idea </i>of what you will be like. Aspects imply things about demeanor, appearance, and (often latent) skills. They also demonstrate the nature of your power, such that it is essentially different from that of another Aspect. It has almost nothing to do with your expected role. A Fire Aspect is not guaranteed to be a fighter. He might be a socialite. Aspect says so little about the differences in Dragon-Blooded that you can expect similar roles from all of them. They are inherently soldiers, inherently group-arrayed, and inherently familial.<br /> <br /> Castes say a lot more. Castes are fixed. You do not fall out of Castes. [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I would say Lunars need to have Aspects, not Castes. They are all about fluidity and transcending borders, so even if they are &quot;No moon Aspect, Full moon,&quot; etc. it's more of a guideline and very much a weaker definition. Compared to the Solars, which are rigid.<br /> <br /> I mean, just even think about with their related magical materials: Orichalcum is rigid, Moonsilver is a literal liquid. (quasi-liquid? Non-Newtonian fluid?)<br /> <br /> <br /> I was going to say &quot;end my argument.&quot; <i>However</i>, I just realized that Aspect can mean another thing: that you are <i>part </i>and <i>directly related</i> to something, as opposed to<i> cast</i> (har har, puns) into place by an external force. This makes sense for Dragonbloods, as they claim direct lineage to the Dragons (If I get their religion right,) so they are not just <i>Chosen</i> of the Dragons, they are <i>part</i> of the Dragons...in blood and parentage. For a Lunar, that type of Aspect doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> *shrugs*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T20:10:40-08:00","id":44627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44554#post44554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Aspect connotes very little beyond an<i> idea </i>of what you will be like. Aspects imply things about demeanor, appearance, and (often latent) skills. They also demonstrate the nature of your power, such that it is essentially different from that of another Aspect. It has almost nothing to do with your expected role. A Fire Aspect is not guaranteed to be a fighter. He might be a socialite. Aspect says so little about the differences in Dragon-Blooded that you can expect similar roles from all of them. They are inherently soldiers, inherently group-arrayed, and inherently familial.<br /> <br /> Castes say a lot more. Castes are fixed. You do not fall out of Castes. It is not expected that a Dawn will be something other than a fighter. Castes align with the person you were before Exaltation. Characters can deviate from Castes, but it is very rare that they simply cease to operate within their definitions. Meanwhile, Dragon-Blooded are not deliberately Chosen for their skills and talents. They are an outgrowth of their parents' (and their parents') Aspects, and so they inherit blood traits, and those are expressed when they come into their own Aspects. Denying an Aspect is not essentially possible because Aspects intermingle in the blood, just as traits of the parents mingle to create children. Dragon-Blooded have flex. Solars do not. They are not inheriting anything so much as they are exemplifying who they always were to begin with. Castes are an extremely strong predictor for roles and social placement as only persons who would fit those roles are Chosen in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on this... I think Aspects are wholly inappropriate for the Lunar Exalted as I currently understand them. The Lunar Exalted's capability to control their form and the approaches they take towards solving the problems they face present a large problem for a descriptor that is based on things such as 'demeanor' or 'appearance' or even skills that can be latent. For example, no Lunar was born knowing how to fly, but by being able to take the shape of a bird, they overcome this inability. From my understanding, to give the Lunar Exalted Aspects would be to contradict this definition, unless the Lunar Exalted were to be changed so wholly that you've effectively changed the only coherent characteristics they've had over the two previous editions.<br /> <br /> Based on current knowledge of the Lunar Exalted... Castes are much more appropriate. As you define, Castes are fixed. You do not fall out of Castes. This makes the event of the Lunar Exalted losing their Castes as being such a shocking tragedy to the Lunar Exalted. It's very symbolic of the Lunar Exalted being cast out from Creation proper, from losing their previously held stations in the First Age. They've lost their station, they've lost their status, they've lost their purpose! The breaking of the Castes is the twist of the knife in a long string of tragedies they've previously suffered. It is the mystical representation of everything the Lunar Exalted previously knew and stood for, being taken away from them.<br /> <br /> And that's why I think it's important for the Lunar Exalted to keep with having Castes. It emphasizes that even when beaten, when broken, when exiled, when made to be outcasts and monsters, when stripped of their responsibilities and their duties, that they've reforged their own Castes. It is the Lunar Exalted's collective resilience, cunning and genius that allowed them to give themselves a new purpose. In the First Age, they stood with the Exalted Host, but when exiled and reviled in the Age of Sorrows, the Lunar Exalted now stand on their own.<br /> <br /> It's a story of tragedy, suffering, strength and pride. These would be people who bear scars of the blows that should have killed them, but didn't, and now it's their turn to strike.<br /> <br /> This story could be completely removed in 3rd Edition, but that would be a great disappointment to me if it did. It's one of the best, glorious things about them.<br /> <br /> Also, I've always felt that Dragon-Blooded Aspects are much more restrictive than Solar Castes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T20:22:11-08:00","id":44632,"title":"","content":"I think my answer becomes contingent upon how fixed Aspects are as viewed through the prism of Lunars. If all they have to do in order to change Aspects is get new tattoos that's an interesting new level of flexibility for them I would find agreeable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T20:24:40-08:00","id":44634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44627#post44627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on current knowledge of the Lunar Exalted... Castes are much more appropriate. As you define, Castes are fixed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like how we read the exact same thing and came to the complete opposite conclusion. XD<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T20:30:44-08:00","id":44635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=43583#post43583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Castes/aspects/etc. serve two main purposes. First and most importantly, they\u2019re there to give structure to an Exalt type to make them more interesting to the player and to facilitate character creation. Second, they\u2019re useful shorthand to describe characters: knowing that you\u2019re up against \u201ca Dawn and a Twilight\u201d is a lot more evocative and informative than \u201ctwo Solars\u201d. When you\u2019re discussing how to divide Lunars, your priorities should be into making them as interesting and easy to parse as possible.<br /> <br /> I could write an entire essay on why Lunar Castes are shit, but I\u2019ll be brief and boil it down to three things: they\u2019re overly restrictive, they\u2019re unclear, and there\u2019s too few of them. Let\u2019s hit the points one by one.<br /> <br /> First off, remember that the main purpose of a Caste/Aspect/Whatever is to provide a structure that\u2019s evocative and makes creating the character you want easier. What the Caste provides is a skeleton that you build around: it\u2019s the marrow, not the meat of what you are. For Solars, a player who is into all of his Caste Stuff and defines himself narrowly according to it is very unusual: the Castes are designed to be used so that you create \u201ca Zenith leader <i>who is also a master swordsman and has an abiding interest in finding and translating old texts\u201d</i> or \u201ca Twilight craftsman <i>who uses clever gadgets to hunt and kill the minions of Malfeas in Chiaroscuro\u201d</i>. The Caste is not who you are or what you do. The Caste is about you having a core aptitude for a certain number of things that you can raise to 5 immediately and learn cool Charms for.<br /> Lunar Castes are a straightjacket. They lock you very firmly into a McCombo package of Attributes with redundant competencies that say very firmly \u201cyou are physical/mental/social-focused\u201d. The inability to raise Attributes instantly (as Solars do with Abilities) and the high cost of raising them, the higher cost of unfavored Charms (everything outside your narrow Caste McCombo), and the fact that the system encourages specialization means that players are punished very harshly for stepping beyond the archetype\u2014for making your character interesting! The 3 Caste / 1 Favored spread is one of the dumbest things in Lunars.<br /> <br /> Second, Lunar Castes are simultaneously about Attribute lines (Physical/Social/Mental) and about roles (Warrior/Trickster/Shaman). Physical/Social/Mental as the basis of Castes is crap, because it\u2019s about as evocative as an engineering manual. Other than surface symmetry (which should never be your main design criteria) there are no good reasons whatsoever to associate Lunar archetypes to the Attribute lines. Any reworking of Castes should address this as a priority.<br /> Warrior/Trickster/Shaman is better, but still problematic. \u2018Warrior\u2019 on its own is not good enough: it\u2019s too generic and stale (fun exercise: picture the Solar Castes being called Warrior/Priest/Wizard/Rogue/Bard). From a systems design standpoint it\u2019s also a problem: for a game that is as heavily combat-centric as Exalted (compare the pagecount devoted to combat v. that for any other system aspect), presenting one of the options as the superior combat option is a mistake. The fact that a Twilight (Scholar) can match the Dawn (General) in combat is an important feature. \u2018Shaman\u2019 is also weird\u2014what is it that they do, again? Commune with nature and pray to spirits? Is this kind of thing even in their Charmset? Is there any Lunar that shows what it means to be a Shaman anywhere in the Exalted line?<br /> <br /> Third, three base archetypes is too little. Other than sticking to Attribute lines for surface symmetry, which I\u2019ve already condemned as stupid, there\u2019s no reason to limit Lunars to three castes. Alchemicals, which are also Attribute-based, get six and are the better for it. Most other Exalted types get five, which affords players a much greater variety in terms of what kind of Caste (skeleton) they want to build their characters around. Whether we go for Castes (e.g., \u2018Hunter\u2019, \u2018Trickster\u2019, \u2018Leader\u2019, \u2018Spy\u2019) or Aspects (this would be a hell of a lot easier if Lunars didn\u2019t have a personal animal totem), three archetypes isn\u2019t enough to cover the spectrum of cool characters you can build using the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like BPM notes, castes and aspects serve as a starting point for character design. And I agree that the Lunar castes are a bit problematic in that respect. The main reason for that is that their story doesn't line up with their mechanics again. I mean, in 2e being good at physical things meant that you could be a good warrior, but you could also be a good blacksmith, a good burglar, or a good athlete. And it doesn't help you at all with being a good warleader or tactician (not that those fields were well served by 2e's mechanics either...)<br /> <br /> And Tricksters and Shamen generally both need some attributes from all three. It also doesn't help that, if you define Shaman as someone with arcane knowledge who treats with spirits, the guys who have that baked into their charmset are Sidereals, not Lunars.<br /> <br /> Thus, to do those three castes, you would need to go back and reallocate the attributes and everything.<br /> <br /> <br /> However, in the spirit of this thread, I'm curious what people would think of Lunars who had the Physical Aspect, Mental Aspect, and Social Aspect? While I grant this is a bit technical, it could be interesting to have a type of character who was all about solving every situation with words and social skills or with their mind or with their body. You would want charms to reinforce this, obviously, by creating charms that allowed the social and mental guys to solve or avoid physical problems with their words and wits and vice versa and everything. They shouldn't be the best charms ever, of course, but just enough so that a Lunar of one caste can legitimately try to achieve most objectives via their chosen paradigm.<br /> <br /> This would be much like how DBs get charms that broaden the boundaries of their abilities, like how Air Aspects have some athletics charms in Stealth. You would want these charms to reinforce the paradigm too. Like you could give Strength a forceful intimidation charm and Dexterity might get a sexy walk charm, but neither of the two attributes would get broad access to the Charisma charms that let you be forceful, sexy, cute, and demure in turn.<br /> <br /> I can already hear someone getting ready to tell me that, while that might be interesting, it's not a big enough skeleton to really work from to build a character concept. And, to be fair, they're right. Fortunately, Lunars have a backup source for that, the Totem. I admit it might take some finagling and probably a decent chunk of the book should be devoted to totems in that case, but being able to go &quot;I'm a Social Focused Werefox&quot; seems like it should be enough of a starting position to build a character around.<br /> <br /> I'll grant too that they should be able to get favored attributes, so they can get outside their paradigm if they need to. I'm not gonna say how many, because that depends on too many other factors in this hypothetical situation that I couldn't even guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T20:57:28-08:00","id":44645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44634#post44634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like how we read the exact same thing and came to the complete opposite conclusion. XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I think... that when communication leads to two completely different conclusions, then there is something being communicated poorly. For instance... Aspects of What? Elements at least have connotations that we can latch onto easily for description. &quot;Fiery&quot; temper, &quot;Stoic&quot; and so forth...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T21:44:22-08:00","id":44667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44589#post44589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When an Alchemical is made, their Caste is chosen based on the nature of their past lives, and their personality reflects those past lives, and thus their Chosen Caste. It is probably because of this deliberate design that Alchemicals do not have Aspects. Liminals get Aspects because of the accidental nature of their birth, in becoming something their creators did not intend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, this is a really good pair of foils.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals are made, but it's wrong to think of that making as the origin point. Their bodies are constructed to align with the people they had been in their prior incarnations and will continue to be. There is very much a continuity of who they are before and after, and it is the choices they made and people they grew to be that brought them there. Castes are the best fit.<br /> <br /> Liminals are made and that making really <i>is</i> the origin point of the person, if not of the history. There are some things about them that have been defined and shaped by their bodies'/parts' prior owners and their creators, much like how all children have had some things defined and shaped by their parents (hello again, Terrestrial connection!). Aspects are the best fit.<br /> <br /> Though the idea of birth/origin is seductive as a determining trait, choosing it as one may be a mistake. Consider Sidereals, who carry their Exaltations from birth. Hypothetical Sidereal Aspects instead of Castes would have each Star-Chosen inherently inclined toward behavior marked by journeys, serenity, war, secrets or endings. This is not so in Sidereals, though it's an easy mistake to make. Those Chosen not yet Exalted are people like any others, but their Exaltations ensure their lives will shape and mold and prepare them to be people appropriate for their respective Castes. Joybringers aren't Exalted for <i>being</i> joyous, they're Exalted for <i>understanding</i> joy, and for knowing (or being equipped to know) how best to create, reduce, use, and otherwise interact with joy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T21:50:27-08:00","id":44671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44645#post44645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think... that when communication leads to two completely different conclusions, then there is something being communicated poorly. For instance... Aspects of What? Elements at least have connotations that we can latch onto easily for description. &quot;Fiery&quot; temper, &quot;Stoic&quot; and so forth...</div> </div> </div> </div>The moon.<br /> <br /> I mean, both Solar and Lunar Castes <i>already</i> use the sun and moon as elaborate metaphors for their caste roles. Turning the Lunar Castes into Aspects just means that the metaphor can be broadened, made more flexible, more inclusive. The symbols and metaphors of each Aspect need not no longer be shoehorned into the Caste roles of Warrior, Trickster, and Loremaster. Rather, any of those three roles, and many others besides, can follow from the symbolism of any Aspect.<br /> <br /> For example, the light of the Full Moon has been be associated with the following by various cultures on Earth, in no particular order: revelation, lunacy, madness, berserker rage, lust, longing, passion, beauty, guidance, justice, thieves, magic, love.<br /> <br /> The changing of the moon can stand for liminality, in-between states, twilight, mercuriality, deceptiveness, whimsy, transformation, the unexpected, spontaneity, etc.<br /> <br /> The new moon can take on connotations of doubt and uncertainty, the unknown and the fear thereof, mysterious shapes lurking just beyond the light, the wonders and horrors to be found off the beaten path, away from the safe and the known and the named.<br /> <br /> Note that each of these can easily assume the any of the roles we associate with the current Lunar Castes within its particular thematic niche. The Full Moon has aspects of revelation and mysteries unveiled, as well as madness and violence and powerful emotions (and the manipulation thereof, presumably). The Changing Moon includes aspects of the walker-between-worlds and the Deadly Beastman Transformation as well as the shapeshifting trickster. The No Moon includes aspects of the unnameable horror, the Monster, the blood-soaked Beast, as well as the bogeyman and the mischief-making spirit and the keeper of secret lore. And all that's just the tip of the iceberg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:05:01-08:00","id":44682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44671#post44671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The moon.<br /> <br /> I mean, both Solar and Lunar Castes <i>already</i> use the sun and moon as elaborate metaphors for their caste roles. Turning the Lunar Castes into Aspects just means that the metaphor can be broadened, made more flexible, more inclusive. The symbols and metaphors of each Aspect need not no longer be shoehorned into the Caste roles of Warrior, Trickster, and Loremaster. Rather, any of those three roles, and many others besides, can follow from the symbolism of any Aspect.<br /> <br /> For example, the light of the Full Moon has been be associated with the following by various cultures on Earth, in no particular order: revelation, lunacy, madness, berserker rage, lust, longing, passion, beauty, guidance, justice, thieves, magic, love.<br /> <br /> The changing of the moon can stand for liminality, in-between states, twilight, mercuriality, deceptiveness, whimsy, transformation, the unexpected, spontaneity, etc.<br /> <br /> The new moon can take on connotations of doubt and uncertainty, the unknown and the fear thereof, mysterious shapes lurking just beyond the light, the wonders and horrors to be found off the beaten path, away from the safe and the known and the named.<br /> <br /> Note that each of these can easily assume the any of the roles we associate with the current Lunar Castes within its particular thematic niche. The Full Moon has aspects of revelation and mysteries unveiled, as well as madness and violence and powerful emotions (and the manipulation thereof, presumably). The Changing Moon includes aspects of the walker-between-worlds and the Deadly Beastman Transformation as well as the shapeshifting trickster. The No Moon includes aspects of the unnameable horror, the Monster, the blood-soaked Beast, as well as the bogeyman and the mischief-making spirit and the keeper of secret lore. And all that's just the tip of the iceberg.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds incredibly chaotic, which is not conductive to the systemic grouping with clear definitions that enable players to point to the specific Exalt type division that they want to express with their character. We have to keep in mind that this is for a Roleplaying Game, with mechanics and rules to present a structure that enables the players to tell the stories they want, and if people scratch their heads in confusion to what defines the specifics of an Exalt type, then that will only be harmful to the express purpose of designing a game.<br /> <br /> Lunars have been screwed over hard in the past by having an incoherent theme to them. At least the three Castes provided you with structure to base a character around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:33:43-08:00","id":44696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44671#post44671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, the light of the Full Moon has been be associated with the following by various cultures on Earth, in no particular order: revelation, lunacy, madness, berserker rage, lust, longing, passion, beauty, guidance, justice, thieves, magic, love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is all well and good, but Exalted holds that the Waning Moon is the maddening collection of phases. The Full Moon is more like the full moon in the Umbral Realm of Pangaea in W:TA - you can see, so you can hunt. There is no mention of madness, but due to its associations with Beloved Cattelesta, it might be associated with self-sacrifice and willingness to aid others above your own interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:40:12-08:00","id":44697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44627#post44627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on current knowledge of the Lunar Exalted... Castes are much more appropriate. As you define, Castes are fixed. You do not fall out of Castes. This makes the event of the Lunar Exalted losing their Castes as being such a shocking tragedy to the Lunar Exalted. It's very symbolic of the Lunar Exalted being cast out from Creation proper, from losing their previously held stations in the First Age. They've lost their station, they've lost their status, they've lost their purpose! The breaking of the Castes is the twist of the knife in a long string of tragedies they've previously suffered. It is the mystical representation of everything the Lunar Exalted previously knew and stood for, being taken away from them.<br /> <br /> And that's why I think it's important for the Lunar Exalted to keep with having Castes. It emphasizes that even when beaten, when broken, when exiled, when made to be outcasts and monsters, when stripped of their responsibilities and their duties, that they've reforged their own Castes. It is the Lunar Exalted's collective resilience, cunning and genius that allowed them to give themselves a new purpose. In the First Age, they stood with the Exalted Host, but when exiled and reviled in the Age of Sorrows, the Lunar Exalted now stand on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like much of what you're saying, and agree Castes feel more appropriate for Lunars. It's also put a hypothetical notion into my head, and I'm unsure how I feel about it. I'd be curious to know what others think.<br /> <br /> Suppose the term &quot;Lost Castes&quot; is not taken to mean Lunars lost some of their Castes or even that they lost all and forged new ones in place of the old, but that Lunars no longer have Castes at all. They have changed their Exaltations so significantly -- and precisely in accordance with their aims -- that they possess Aspects instead. Potential was seen in the Aspects they could create, potential that would make the Lunar Host as a whole better suited to overturning the Realm than potential Castes they saw. Perhaps their plan is/was to redefine themselves yet again when they rule Creation. But for now, the traits of the Aspects continue to seem the best bet toward that end.<br /> <br /> Hrrmm... Maybe just because it feels so very vague, but after writing it, I'm pretty sure I'd rather this not be canon. Could be interesting to see in a Shard, though. Maybe if I had a keener grasp on what possibilities Lunar Aspects might present versus Lunar Castes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:56:42-08:00","id":44705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44697#post44697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like much of what you're saying, and agree Castes feel more appropriate for Lunars. It's also put a hypothetical notion into my head, and I'm unsure how I feel about it. I'd be curious to know what others think.<br /> <br /> Suppose the term &quot;Lost Castes&quot; is not taken to mean Lunars lost some of their Castes or even that they lost all and forged new ones in place of the old, but that Lunars no longer have Castes at all. They have changed their Exaltations so significantly -- and precisely in accordance with their aims -- that they possess Aspects instead. Potential was seen in the Aspects they could create, potential that would make the Lunar Host as a whole better suited to overturning the Realm than potential Castes they saw. Perhaps their plan is/was to redefine themselves yet again when they rule Creation. But for now, the traits of the Aspects continue to seem the best bet toward that end.<br /> <br /> Hrrmm... Maybe just because it feels so very vague, but after writing it, I'm pretty sure I'd rather this not be canon. Could be interesting to see in a Shard, though. Maybe if I had a keener grasp on what possibilities Lunar Aspects might present versus Lunar Castes...</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, we've only got one example of Aspects to go on and those Aspects are based on... well, a pretty concrete and well trodden ground. Earth, Air, Fire, Water and Wood. Wood is a bit of the odd ball from those, but the game does a good job of defining what context and meaning &quot;Wood&quot; has. There's also supplemental references to draw inspiration from for these Elements. Avatar: The Last Airbender gives great inspiration on fighting styles and aesthetics for fighting that is meant to evoke the four classical elements. How exactly would we define the Lunar Aspects? <br /> <br /> It's all well and good to have a character type based on being chaotic and mercurial, but that is a bad thing when you lose your audience, when they look at you all puzzled and say, &quot;Well... What does that mean you can play as a Lunar?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T23:58:51-08:00","id":44744,"title":"","content":"I can see potential for Lunars to have either Castes or Aspects. It's mostly a question of which direction the writers choose to take them.<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel like Aspects work a little better than Castes. An Aspect is some core piece of the Exalt that never changes, and that is exactly what a Lunar needs. They might be a mighty warrior one day, and a king the next. Or perhaps the day after that they are a merchant. A Caste doesn't make sense, but an Aspect creates an anchor. Something for the Lunar to fall back upon, something that relates to everything they do, no matter what they do. It also makes the Chimera a little more horrifying, as they lack such an anchor. As their desires and whims pull them in every direction their personality fragments. Of course, I have no idea what those Aspects might actually be, so ... uh ... I'll get back to you on that.<br /> <br /> In addition, a Caste is an extension of what you already are. However, some of the earlier comments on Lunars called them, &quot;monsters with some humanity in them, or humans with a monster inside&quot;, which seems to imply (to me anyway) that a character would not necessarily be the same after their Exaltation. You could make Castes fit, but having what is essentially different kinds of roles for different kinds of monsters ... doesn't really feel right. Whereas an Aspect feels like it could describe what kind of monster you are. You aren't compelled to act like a monster, but it's sitting down there, inside you.<br /> <br /> Now I'm just blabbering. Hopefully some of this was useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/242-mindworm-jim","name":"Mindworm Jim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T00:17:13-08:00","id":44751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mindworm Jim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44744#post44744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see potential for Lunars to have either Castes or Aspects. It's mostly a question of which direction the writers choose to take them.<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel like Aspects work a little better than Castes. An Aspect is some core piece of the Exalt that never changes, and that is exactly what a Lunar needs. They might be a mighty warrior one day, and a king the next. Or perhaps the day after that they are a merchant. A Caste doesn't make sense, but an Aspect creates an anchor. Something for the Lunar to fall back upon, something that relates to everything they do, no matter what they do. It also makes the Chimera a little more horrifying, as they lack such an anchor. As their desires and whims pull them in every direction their personality fragments. Of course, I have no idea what those Aspects might actually be, so ... uh ... I'll get back to you on that.<br /> <br /> In addition, a Caste is an extension of what you already are. However, some of the earlier comments on Lunars called them, &quot;monsters with some humanity in them, or humans with a monster inside&quot;, which seems to imply (to me anyway) that a character would not necessarily be the same after their Exaltation. You could make Castes fit, but having what is essentially different kinds of roles for different kinds of monsters ... doesn't really feel right. Whereas an Aspect feels like it could describe what kind of monster you are. You aren't compelled to act like a monster, but it's sitting down there, inside you.<br /> <br /> Now I'm just blabbering. Hopefully some of this was useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the difference between &quot;roles for different kinds of monsters&quot; and &quot;what kind of monster you are&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T00:33:37-08:00","id":44756,"title":"","content":"First, a slight sidetracking: Sidereals are not born to their Exaltations, they are fated for it, as far as I know. The difference is: they will not receive their Exaltations because of who they are but because of what they do. The other Sidereals only start training them early (usually) but their Exaltation does come still from their actions and deeds. That is my take on it at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> One issue I have with putting more emhpasis on totem animals: it draws away from Luna as a patron. The devs have mentioned that the Lunars connection with animals is due to Luna and Gaia's relationship (or something like that). Puitting more emphasis on animals pulls the Lunars more towards Gaia than Luna, imho. Not sure how to solve that though, but I'd like to put more emphasis on Luna's nature as a nightmare of a Primoridal, or god, not sure which. Again, no concrete idea where to go with that though<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T01:28:11-08:00","id":44764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44751#post44751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the difference between &quot;roles for different kinds of monsters&quot; and &quot;what kind of monster you are&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, yeah, that didn't really come out very well. Let's see if I can do better ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Castes are fixed. You do not fall out of Castes. It is not expected that a Dawn will be something other than a fighter. Castes align with the person you were before Exaltation. Characters can deviate from Castes, but it is very rare that they simply cease to operate within their definitions. </div> </div> </div>The way I read this description, Castes strike me as something of an external feature. Your Caste is a circle in the ground around you. How you operate or what you do within that circle can vary greatly, and you may occasionally step out of the circle for some reason or another, but you will eventually return. It's too ... I guess 'structured' is the best word ... for what are supposed to be primal and savage beings caught somewhere between human and monster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An Aspect connotes very little beyond an idea of what you will be like. Aspects imply things about demeanor, appearance, and (often latent) skills. They also demonstrate the nature of your power, such that it is essentially different from that of another Aspect. It has almost nothing to do with your expected role. </div> </div> </div>This, on the other hand, strikes me as very internal. The Aspect is a starting point, nothing more. You can do whatever you want, but whatever you do will be built upon the foundation the Aspect gives you. Coloring it, supporting it, undermining it, whatever. This strikes me as a superior method to represent the human/monster dichotomy that they seem to be aiming for with Lunars. Your monstrousness does not force you into one particular path, but it influences the outcome of any path you walk.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is all based off of one comment that may have changed, or may simply not have been very important. So who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/242-mindworm-jim","name":"Mindworm Jim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T12:23:28-08:00","id":45054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44696#post44696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is all well and good, but Exalted holds that the Waning Moon is the maddening collection of phases. The Full Moon is more like the full moon in the Umbral Realm of Pangaea in W:TA - you can see, so you can hunt. There is no mention of madness, but due to its associations with Beloved Cattelesta, it might be associated with self-sacrifice and willingness to aid others above your own interests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44671#post44671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The symbols and metaphors of each Aspect need no longer be shoehorned into the Caste roles of Warrior, Trickster, and Loremaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point is that the Full Moon no longer would need to be limited to that set-up. Instead of coming at it from the perspective of &quot;we need some moon-symbolism to tie into fighty-type Caste roles&quot;, Lunar Aspects could be approached from a perspective of &quot;here are the themes and symbolism suggested by this aspect of the moon. What kinds of characters follow from that?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44682#post44682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sounds incredibly chaotic, which is not conductive to the systemic grouping with clear definitions that enable players to point to the specific Exalt type division that they want to express with their character. We have to keep in mind that this is for a Roleplaying Game, with mechanics and rules to present a structure that enables the players to tell the stories they want, and if people scratch their heads in confusion to what defines the specifics of an Exalt type, then that will only be harmful to the express purpose of designing a game.<br /> <br /> Lunars have been screwed over hard in the past by having an incoherent theme to them. At least the three Castes provided you with structure to base a character around.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44671#post44671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the light of the Full Moon has been be associated with the following by various cultures on Earth, in no particular order:<b> revelation,</b> lunacy, <b>madness, berserker rage, lust, longing, passion,</b> beauty, guidance,<b> justice,</b> thieves, magic, <b>love.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44671#post44671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Full Moon has aspects of <b>revelation and mysteries unveiled</b>, as well as <b>madness and violence and powerful emotions.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44671#post44671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The changing of the moon can stand for <b>liminality, in-between states,</b> twilight, <b>mercuriality, deceptiveness,</b> <b>whimsy, transformation, the unexpected,</b> spontaneity, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44671#post44671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Changing Moon includes aspects of the <b>walker-between-worlds</b> and the Deadly Beastman <b>Transformation</b> as well as the <b>shapeshifting trickster.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44671#post44671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new moon can take on connotations of <b>doubt and uncertainty, the unknown </b>and the <b>fear</b> thereof, <b>mysterious shapes lurking just beyond the light,</b> the<b> wonders and horrors</b> to be found <b>off the beaten path, away from the safe and the known and the named.</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=44671#post44671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The No Moon includes aspects of the <b>unnameable horror,</b> the <b>Monster,</b> the blood-soaked <b>Beast,</b> as well as the <b>bogeyman</b> and the mischief-making <b>spirit</b> and the keeper of <b>secret lore.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>As you can see, there's plenty of structure here to base a character around. I may have hammered on the point that any of the three proposed Aspects could play the role of any of the Castes, but do not mistake this for meaning that they are <i>interchangeable</i> or <i>indistinguishable</i>. Each brings its own approach, its own characteristic style and tone, to the table.<br /> <br /> The Full Moon, as a Warrior, is a furious berserker or a hot-blooded avenger or a self-appointed dispenser of justice. As a Trickster, he is a seducer, relying on animal magnetism and sheer audacity to get away with his escapades. As a Lorekeeper, he's the one who shines light into dark places and rips away lies and deception...or else tears away the veils concealing That Which Man Was Not Meant To Know. There's always a sense of energy, of power, of force and motion and vitality in the way he does things.<br /> <br /> The Changing Moon Warrior is fluid and flowing, both in motion and in form. He doesn't restrict himself to just one war-form--no, he's the one who will slip between a dozen shapes over the course of the fight, and whose flesh flows out of your grasp just as you think you've finally got him. And he's a Trickster in the tradition of Coyote or Raven or Br'er Rabbit, a shapeshifting thing from the wild who plays impossible pranks and jokes just because he can and who's always one step ahead of anyone who thinks they've managed to catch him. And as a Lorekeeper he's the outsider, the walker-between-worlds, the shaman, neither wholly of this world nor wholly of the other.<br /> <br /> The No Moon Warrior is the monster you're afraid of. He's a thing unseen and unknown, a nightmare come to life, striking from the shadows and vanishing before you catch more than a terrified glimpse. Or he's the one hunting such a monster: the lone hunter who knows the secret weakness of the unstoppable beast. As a Trickster he's a bogeyman, a thing of fairy tales and campfire stories, something from outside the world of the comfortable and the known that plays by rules and judges by standards and acts for reasons unknown and unknowable to you, a thing strange and inexplicable and mysterious. And the Lorekeeper No Moon knows all of the secrets and mysteries and wonders and horrors that lie hidden beyond the campfire's light, and might choose to share some of them. Or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T14:39:45-08:00","id":45135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=45054#post45054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Full Moon, as a Warrior, is a furious berserker or a hot-blooded avenger or a self-appointed dispenser of justice. As a Trickster, he is a seducer, relying on animal magnetism and sheer audacity to get away with his escapades. As a Lorekeeper, he's the one who shines light into dark places and rips away lies and deception...or else tears away the veils concealing That Which Man Was Not Meant To Know. There's always a sense of energy, of power, of force and motion and vitality in the way he does things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. What Attributes would Full Moon naturally favor, to convey this?<br /> <br /> Intelligence, Charisma, and Strength or Stamina?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Changing Moon Warrior is fluid and flowing, both in motion and in form. He doesn't restrict himself to just one war-form--no, he's the one who will slip between a dozen shapes over the course of the fight, and whose flesh flows out of your grasp just as you think you've finally got him. And he's a Trickster in the tradition of Coyote or Raven or Br'er Rabbit, a shapeshifting thing from the wild who plays impossible pranks and jokes just because he can and who's always one step ahead of anyone who thinks they've managed to catch him. And as a Lorekeeper he's the outsider, the walker-between-worlds, the shaman, neither wholly of this world nor wholly of the other. </div> </div> </div>Dexterity, Manipulation, Wits or Perception?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The No Moon Warrior is the monster you're afraid of. He's a thing unseen and unknown, a nightmare come to life, striking from the shadows and vanishing before you catch more than a terrified glimpse. Or he's the one hunting such a monster: the lone hunter who knows the secret weakness of the unstoppable beast. As a Trickster he's a bogeyman, a thing of fairy tales and campfire stories, something from outside the world of the comfortable and the known that plays by rules and judges by standards and acts for reasons unknown and unknowable to you, a thing strange and inexplicable and mysterious. And the Lorekeeper No Moon knows all of the secrets and mysteries and wonders and horrors that lie hidden beyond the campfire's light, and might choose to share some of them. Or not. </div> </div> </div>Whatever's left.<br /> <br /> Perception or Wits, Appearance, Strength?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T16:44:48-08:00","id":45909,"title":"","content":"Some of the prior lore about how Lunar Castes work, combined with some assumptions about new priorities in this Edition, feel like they might imply some things about suitability of Castes for Lunars.<br /> <br /> There's the idea that the way Lunars used to work was that they Exalted first and then got a Caste later as it naturally affixed itself to their talents, which changed into the Castes breaking up a bit and needing to be fixed by tattoos, and there are indications that there's going to be an idea towards greater emphasis on Lunar relations to Solars in their original form as contrasted against their new context.<br /> <br /> Now, one thing I could take from the unfixed nature of the Lunar Caste is that it could imply the roles carried by such a Caste are a bit different to other ones. A Solar can be somebody who was a great warrior (or had a strong inclination towards pursuing or resolving things through contest and the like) and then they're Exalted to be the Caste that includes warriors as part of an overall martial excellence archetype because Solars are built around that general Appolonian arete thing. A Sidereal destined to aid the progression of notable conveyances gets the Journeys Caste, an Alchemical made out of lives of inspirational leadership and high-minded experimentation becomes an Orichalcum Caste*. They're roles defined by the general context of what that Exalt does.<br /> <br /> So it could be that, with Lunars, if part of what makes them up is that storm of persona and wild energy that makes for the whole &quot;monster/good person&quot; dichotomy, well... it might be that the role you're suited for as a Lunar can only really become apparent after you've spent some time being a Lunar, because it might be that Lunars have the biggest transition between what they were before and after they Exalted.<br /> <br /> I'm just thinking, right now, it would seem fairly suitable to the differences between Lunars and the others, especially Solars, as well as for helping character concepts be a bit more open. I mean, the monster inside a good person inside a monster thing feels interesting, but it also feels like it would be fairly limiting if you had to assume that the only people who became Lunars were, well, Holden made the comparison to Dexter once.<br /> <br /> I look at Seven Devil Clever and think &quot;what if she did that same impressive ballsy thing that got Luna's attention, and then got Exalted out of it, and <i>then</i> she's got this monstrous storm inside of her&quot;, because Seven Devil Clever is fun and straightforward and her current origin story doesn't really imply anything of being Dexter.<br /> <br /> And then she's got this new characteristic, and has to feel it out before anybody can figure out what Lunar Caste suits her.<br /> <br /> In the First Age, this probably would have included how she relates to and synergizes with her Mate, and that leads into the whole big thing of Solar-Lunar issues right there.<br /> <br /> In the Second Age, it might come out of what aptitudes and proclivities she directs towards the usurpers and other enemies of the Silver Pact, in which case, given what we might gather of the Lunar methodology there, &quot;Warrior, Trickster and Shaman&quot; seems a fairly pertinent divide. Might also help give some weight to the idea that tinkering around with their Exaltations was an achievement and a big deal for the Silver Pact.<br /> <br /> If Lunars had Aspects, I'd say they'd have to have them set up from the start, and maybe even bridge them off of what actual phase of the moon you Exalted under (time of day notwithstanding), and then build up from there. Because the ultimate difference between Aspect and Caste seems to be what side of the character generation they're on**; you start with Aspect and then figure out what the person makes of it, whereas you start with aptitudes and achievements and thus assign a Caste based on that.<br /> <br /> * Incidentally, Alchemical Castes are assigned the same way that every other Caste is in Autochthonia, and they're Castes built around the unique and necessary place Alchemicals have in Autochthonian society. The Octet needs its inspirational visionaries and personable industrial czars as much as it needs its therapists and clerics and laborers. <br /> ** I mean this as an analogy rather than a literal approach to character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T17:13:27-08:00","id":45927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=45909#post45909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's the idea that the way Lunars used to work was that they Exalted first and then got a Caste later as it naturally affixed itself to their talents [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you get that idea? I don't recognise it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [...] Holden made the comparison to Dexter once. </div> </div> </div>The point of that comparison was that they're <i>not</i> Dexter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T18:18:39-08:00","id":45960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=45927#post45927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did you get that idea? I don't recognise it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In First Edition, the Lunar Exalted always needed rituals of some sort to do the job, revolving around a Wyld Quest. Those methods no longer worked after the Wyld Taint, and so they developed the Tattoos.<br /> <br /> Second Edition took the tack that Lunar Castes, before the Wyld Taint, would naturally settle into the appropriate Caste on their own after a time, with rituals of any kind being unnecessary.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point of that comparison was that they're <i>not</i> Dexter. </div> </div> </div>That's what they said, yes. Whatever they meant by &quot;good person with a monster inside&quot; or &quot;monster with a good person inside&quot;, Holden was explicit that this did not mean something like Dexter.<br /> <br /> I think it means &quot;Wolverine, with his inner beast&quot; and &quot;John Talbain, with his inner man&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T07:01:50-08:00","id":46227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=45927#post45927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of that comparison was that they're <i>not</i> Dexter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know? Why else would I posit an idea specifically to service Lunars who aren't Dexter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T07:37:17-08:00","id":46246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=46227#post46227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know? Why else would I posit an idea specifically to service Lunars who aren't Dexter?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see what you meant now that you've said something, but -- like MG it seems -- the impression I got on reading was that you had maybe misremembered the quote. It seemed you thought Dexter was the current thing they had in mind and you were lobbying for something broader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T17:54:33-08:00","id":46628,"title":"","content":"As a semi-random aside, the breaking and fixing of the Castes needs to remain a thing in 3e, if only because it's the only unambiguously Lunar owned accomplishment they've had since 1e. Yes, it's context probably needs to change a bit, to stop making their exaltations sound like they were made from sub-par materials, but I like the general idea of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T18:42:34-08:00","id":46661,"title":"","content":"I feel like the breaking of the Castes could have been less troublesome in First Edition when, as far as I know, there wasn't some overriding proscription on the perishability of Exaltations and the abstractions for how the Wyld did its thing might not have been so broad as to fall under a single blanket immunity and the Wyld itself was more vast and fearsome. It might have been feasible that Solars also might have been messed up by prolonged exposure to the Wyld, or various other forces, although maybe not because that might still lead into an undesirable mindset of strictly universalizing Exalts.<br /> <br /> Though if they're going with tying Castes into Solars, that's probably better anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T19:13:28-08:00","id":46676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=46628#post46628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a semi-random aside, the breaking and fixing of the Castes needs to remain a thing in 3e, if only because it's the only unambiguously Lunar owned accomplishment they've had since 1e. Yes, it's context probably needs to change a bit, to stop making their exaltations sound like they were made from sub-par materials, but I like the general idea of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The jist I'm getting is that instead of some taint and losing three Castes that the Changing Moons aren an amalgation of, Luanrs in 3e are instead more purposeful. The Castes werent' broken because they had weak Exaltations against the Wyld but apparently some process was purposefully done to redefine the way Lunar Exaltation manifests and the three Castes now are their own thing that the creators of the tattoos thought would be better for their insurgency agaisnt the Usurpers.<br /> <br /> It has a lot better tone to it when presented in that sense as a willful act that a desperate patch job and takes the aformentioned &quot;This is ours and go fuck yourselves&quot; and owns it more.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T20:12:46-08:00","id":46697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=46676#post46676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The jist I'm getting is that instead of some taint and losing three Castes that the Changing Moons aren an amalgation of, Luanrs in 3e are instead more purposeful. The Castes werent' broken because they had weak Exaltations against the Wyld but apparently some process was purposefully done to redefine the way Lunar Exaltation manifests and the three Castes now are their own thing that the creators of the tattoos thought would be better for their insurgency agaisnt the Usurpers.<br /> <br /> It has a lot better tone to it when presented in that sense as a willful act that a desperate patch job and takes the aformentioned &quot;This is ours and go fuck yourselves&quot; and owns it more.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind this IF anyone could come up with two entirely different sets of Castes, both of which function, and one of which hardly anyone will ever actually get to play.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the first set of Castes would have been designed for the Primordial War, and that seems like the Castes you want for the Post-Usurpation world.<br /> <br /> Now, if the Post-Primordial War Lunars had created a new set of Castes for the relative peace of the First Age, and then tore those false Castes apart to return to their original Primordial War configuration, that would make sense. The First Age Castes wouldn't even need to be something you'd WANT to use, so they don't have to be very good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T20:27:36-08:00","id":46708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=46628#post46628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a semi-random aside, the breaking and fixing of the Castes needs to remain a thing in 3e, if only because it's the only unambiguously Lunar owned accomplishment they've had since 1e. Yes, it's context probably needs to change a bit, to stop making their exaltations sound like they were made from sub-par materials, but I like the general idea of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, for EX3 the Lunars that were in the Primordial War were different from the Lunars in the First Age, and those Lunars changed again after the Usurpation, into the modern form that will be distinct from the two prior forms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T21:16:43-08:00","id":46735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=46697#post46697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can get behind this IF anyone could come up with two entirely different sets of Castes, both of which function, and one of which hardly anyone will ever actually get to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trivially easy to do. We just design two sets of Castes, and then never release the second one! ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T21:18:15-08:00","id":46737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=46708#post46708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, for EX3 the Lunars that were in the Primordial War were different from the Lunars in the First Age, and those Lunars changed again after the Usurpation, into the modern form that will be distinct from the two prior forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>You recall the gist correctly, and there's even more to it than that. Not to say you were implying otherwise, but it may be worth noting there was no discussion of Castes around this remark. Castes as a component/symptom of these changes remains a very reasonable idea. Especially since they've said definitively that the Lost Castes remain in concept if not in execution.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Primordial War [Lunars] were one thing, in the First Age, something else. When the First Age fell, they went through some major changes, that set them on the road to becoming what they are now. And I foresee a major change in their future\u2014one that sets the tone for their premise in EX3.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is the Castes hatewheel meant, this wouldn't have been the first time Lunars redefined what they were, and the last may yet be ahead of them.<br /> <br /> I'm hesitant to speak up, as it's been some time since Aggiecon so it's fuzzy -- please back me up or call me out, anyone else who was there -- but... Holden implied that the new Lunar caste set-up is something the Lunars deliberately put into place, as what they had during the First Age was completely unsuited to their needs in the Second.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd question any assertion that any non-current Castes <i>need</i> to be playable. Would be a nice bonus if they come up with workable, feasible things for it -- particularly if Lunars redefining themselves again is plausible, more examples would be fantastic. But no, it's not necessary. It's certainly something that needs some serious thought given to it. We just don't need that whole enchilada any more than we need a ton of E6+ Lunar Charms: we need what's relevant for the Lunar Elders that appear (presuming they even still have their original castes) and that's about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Two 'but no's close together is lame and clarifying the quote. 01-12-2014, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T00:31:50-08:00","id":46779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=46628#post46628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a semi-random aside, the breaking and fixing of the Castes needs to remain a thing in 3e, if only because it's the only unambiguously Lunar owned accomplishment they've had since 1e. Yes, it's context probably needs to change a bit, to stop making their exaltations sound like they were made from sub-par materials, but I like the general idea of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree. And I think one method of doing this is by making the Wyld something to really be feared. Making the chaos outside of Creation something people don't dare screw with unless they're extremely powerful or fool--hardy. This has the benefit of making the Solar Exalted, who could carve out swaths of Creation from the chaos of the Wyld more impressive, and the fact that the Lunar Exalted adapted themselves to even survive in that horrifying environment all the more impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T02:59:31-08:00","id":46817,"title":"","content":"I do have strong suspicions that, while the Lunar Castes thing will be changed, and the Wyld might be made more interesting, these facts are unlikely to intersect with each other, as I see fewer reasons to exile Lunars to the Wyld in a new Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T10:21:59-08:00","id":46960,"title":"","content":"I recall what Holden said about Exalted not actually being designed to tell the kind of stories set during the Primordial War or First Age, where the scale of heroic, world-changing actions was very different. So, I guess not having concrete details about the Lunar Castes of previous ages is fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T10:32:01-08:00","id":46963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=46817#post46817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have strong suspicions that, while the Lunar Castes thing will be changed, and the Wyld might be made more interesting, these facts are unlikely to intersect with each other, as I see fewer reasons to exile Lunars to the Wyld in a new Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think that the Lunars/Wyld connection has often been bad for them. In a way it makes sense -- the Wyld shares some of the themes and features that define the Lunar Exalted -- but making them too Wyld-focused, either in the sense of being &quot;of the Wyld&quot; or &quot;Wyld cops&quot;, legitimizes their previous irrelevance to Creation and to Creation-based stories. I don't mind them spending time in the Wyld, because they're the Exalted most suited to it, but I don't think Lunars should be &quot;the Wyld Exalted&quot; for similar reasons to why I wouldn't want Sidereals to be &quot;the Heaven Exalted&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T12:57:37-08:00","id":47014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects?p=46963#post46963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I think that the Lunars/Wyld connection has often been bad for them. In a way it makes sense -- the Wyld shares some of the themes and features that define the Lunar Exalted -- but making them too Wyld-focused, either in the sense of being &quot;of the Wyld&quot; or &quot;Wyld cops&quot;, legitimizes their previous irrelevance to Creation and to Creation-based stories. I don't mind them spending time in the Wyld, because they're the Exalted most suited to it, but I don't think Lunars should be &quot;the Wyld Exalted&quot; for similar reasons to why I wouldn't want Sidereals to be &quot;the Heaven Exalted&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals certainly cannot ever be described as &quot;The Heaven Exalted&quot;, despite Yu-Shan being a significant setting for Creation. You can't really separate Yu-Shan from Creation like you can with Autochthonia. It's extremely significant to Creation and Sidereals, for context, for purpose, for meaning and as a scene to explore and conquer in various ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}